asr-000930
01:01:23.500 --> 01:01:32.120
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We told them na hindi naman po magsasalita ang Senate, ang ating legislatura, kung hindi naman po sila nasaktan.

asr-000931
01:01:32.240 --> 01:01:42.220
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Pero we believe that it was directed po sa ilang officials po sa Executive Department, not exactly sa Senate or sa Congress.

asr-000932
01:01:42.220 --> 01:01:48.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So the term regrettable was not in reference to the—

asr-000933
01:01:48.820 --> 01:01:50.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Statements of Senators.

asr-000934
01:01:51.560 --> 01:01:54.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Just to be clear, because we—

asr-000935
01:01:54.400 --> 01:02:01.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I can understand if the statement is directed at the Executive Department.

asr-000936
01:02:02.120 --> 01:02:05.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Walang problema yun dahil kayo-kayo yun.

asr-000937
01:02:06.440 --> 01:02:07.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: No, Mr. President.

asr-000938
01:02:07.940 --> 01:02:09.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Actually, it wasn't really directed.

asr-000939
01:02:09.620 --> 01:02:14.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: It was just communication, interpretation.

asr-000940
01:02:15.640 --> 01:02:17.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Pero those statements were directed to—

asr-000941
01:02:18.820 --> 01:02:21.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Officials within the Executive Department.

asr-000942
01:02:21.800 --> 01:02:22.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-000943
01:02:22.420 --> 01:02:32.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Well, hopefully, to avoid confusion in the future, the statements perhaps should be more categorical because it simply said,

asr-000944
01:02:33.260 --> 01:02:37.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: whatever personal convictions public officials may hold, and I quote,

asr-000945
01:02:37.940 --> 01:02:40.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: their public platforms carry institutional responsibility.

asr-000946
01:02:40.760 --> 01:02:45.380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So if you read it as it is, and to continue,

asr-000947
01:02:45.520 --> 01:02:47.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: they may not pursue preferred approaches towards—

asr-000948
01:02:48.820 --> 01:02:55.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: China or any other international partner without regard for the consequences on the government's overall policy.

asr-000949
01:02:56.240 --> 01:02:57.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So when you read it,

asr-000950
01:02:59.000 --> 01:03:02.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: you wouldn't know that it's not referring to—

asr-000951
01:03:02.820 --> 01:03:08.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: or it's not clear, at the very least, that you're not referring to the senators who spoke up.

asr-000952
01:03:09.380 --> 01:03:15.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So with this clarification, we thank the good sponsor and the department,

asr-000953
01:03:15.560 --> 01:03:18.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and at least maliwanag, no?

asr-000954
01:03:18.820 --> 01:03:24.060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: When we speak up, speak out as a Senate, as a member of the Philippine Senate,

asr-000955
01:03:24.060 --> 01:03:28.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: on matters of foreign policy, it is because we have a role.

asr-000956
01:03:29.820 --> 01:03:36.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And it is part of our constitutional duty, at least from where we sit.

asr-000957
01:03:37.180 --> 01:03:41.180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And it's clear, precisely because we ratify treaties.

asr-000958
01:03:41.840 --> 01:03:48.060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: How can we ratify treaties if we can't speak about whether we oppose or object?

asr-000959
01:03:48.820 --> 01:03:54.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Correct to or support our foreign policy direction.

asr-000960
01:03:54.740 --> 01:03:56.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I hope that's clarified as well.

asr-000961
01:03:56.380 --> 01:04:00.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And I thank the good secretary and the good sponsor for the clarification.

