02:42:42.650 --> 02:42:57.500
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Thank you very much, Mr. President. We are, of course, we're ready to take up the budget of the Civil Service Commission. May we recognize the sponsor to at least give us an overview of the budget, Mr. President?

asr-003328
02:42:57.500 --> 02:42:59.300
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Senator Erwin Tulfo.

asr-003328-split-2
02:42:59.300 --> 02:43:08.880
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Any objection? Hearing none, consideration of the budget of the Civil Service Commission is in order. Senator Erwin Tulfo, Chairman, is recognized.

asr-003328-split-3
02:43:08.880 --> 02:43:25.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Thank you, Mr. President. Thank you, Majority Floor Leader. To the officials and members of the Civil Service Commission, led by its Chairperson, Attorney Marilyn Baruwayap, and to the Career Executive Service Board,

asr-003329
02:43:25.440 --> 02:43:55.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: led by Chairperson Urduja Alvarado, a pleasant good afternoon to everyone. As the Vice Chairperson of the Subcommittee H of the Committee on Finance, I am pleased to present the proposed budgets of two vital institutions that play an indispensable role in our government's pursuit of an efficient, professional, responsive public service. For Fiscal Year 2027, the proposed total new appropriations of the Civil Service Commission stand at 3.1 billion pesos.

asr-003330
02:43:55.440 --> 02:44:25.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: This is 1 billion lower than its proposed budget under the National Expenditure Program, but higher than the 2.91 billion allocation under the General Appropriations Bill. The additional funding request by the CSC and approved by your subcommittee will be used to augment CSC Central Office MOOE, as well as to provide additional funding for its ICT requirements. Meanwhile, the proposed total new appropriations for the Career or of the Career Executive Service Board for Fiscal Year 2027 amount to 200.8 million pesos,

asr-003331
02:44:25.440 --> 02:44:55.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: which is higher than the amounts provided under both the NEP and the GAB. Your subcommittee likewise approved the CESB's additional budget request of 62 million pesos, which will be used to augment its MOOE and capital outlay requirements. These allocations represent our continuing commitment to strengthening the institutions that develop, nurture,

asr-003332
02:44:55.440 --> 02:45:00.000
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and uphold the quality of our public servants.

asr-003333
02:45:00.000 --> 02:45:08.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Sa madaling sabi, ang pamumuhunan natin sa dalawang institusyon na ito ay pamumuhunan din sa ating mga lingkod bayan.

asr-003334
02:45:08.920 --> 02:45:16.240
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: At kung mas mahusay ang ating mga lingkod bayan, mas mahusay din po ang serbisyong may ibibigay natin sa ating mga kababayan.

asr-003335
02:45:16.240 --> 02:45:29.860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: With these points in mind, I respectfully submit for the body's consideration to propose new appropriations for Fiscal Year 2027 of the Civil Service Commission and the Career Service Executive Board.

asr-003336
02:45:30.440 --> 02:45:40.380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Having said that, Mr. President, this representation is now ready to answer questions related to CSC and CESB budget that our colleagues might profound.

asr-003337
02:45:40.860 --> 02:45:42.520
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Maraming salamat po, Mr. President.

asr-003338
02:45:42.520 --> 02:45:48.580
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you, Senator Erwin Tulfo. Majority Leader?

