Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Go ahead.

asr-004365
03:48:00.840 --> 03:48:03.240
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Hihingi lang natin ng konting briefing yung budget nila,

asr-004366
03:48:03.380 --> 03:48:04.720
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. President, by their sponsor.

asr-004367
03:48:05.120 --> 03:48:07.780
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: May we recognize Senator J.B. Ercito?

asr-004368
03:48:08.120 --> 03:48:09.160
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Budget is hereby

asr-004369
03:48:09.160 --> 03:48:11.100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: considered.

asr-004370
03:48:11.600 --> 03:48:13.280
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Senator J.B. Ercito is recognized.

asr-004371
03:48:14.240 --> 03:48:16.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Mr. President. Thank you, Majority Leader.

asr-004372
03:48:16.920 --> 03:48:18.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: This presentation is honored

asr-004373
03:48:18.180 --> 03:48:19.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to sponsor the proposed

asr-004374
03:48:19.260 --> 03:48:21.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 2027 budget of the Office

asr-004375
03:48:21.940 --> 03:48:23.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: of the President. For the record,

asr-004376
03:48:24.220 --> 03:48:25.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the recommended new appropriations of the

asr-004377
03:48:25.900 --> 03:48:29.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Office of the President is 10,083,518,000

asr-004378
03:48:30.000 --> 03:48:30.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: pesos.

asr-004379
03:48:31.760 --> 03:48:33.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mr. President, we are now ready to answer

asr-004380
03:48:33.480 --> 03:48:35.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: any questions from our colleagues.

asr-004381
03:48:40.120 --> 03:48:41.280
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Senator [unclear]

asr-004382
03:48:41.380 --> 03:48:43.960
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: is busy, so you may proceed

asr-004383
03:48:43.960 --> 03:48:44.740
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: with the motion.

asr-004383-split-2
03:48:44.740 --> 03:48:45.700
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Yes, Mr. President, out of

asr-004384
03:48:45.700 --> 03:48:46.060
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: courtesy,

asr-004385
03:48:47.060 --> 03:48:49.120
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: historically,

asr-004386
03:48:50.040 --> 03:48:51.780
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: mga budget ng Office of the

asr-004387
03:48:51.780 --> 03:48:53.780
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: President, including the budget of the Office

asr-004388
03:48:53.780 --> 03:48:55.680
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: of the Vice President, we give them

asr-004389
03:48:55.680 --> 03:48:56.980
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: due courtesy, Mr. President.

asr-004389-split-2
03:48:56.980 --> 03:48:57.280
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Of course.

asr-004390
03:48:57.280 --> 03:48:59.080
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: With that, I move that we...

asr-004390-split-2
03:48:59.080 --> 03:48:59.520
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Most specially

asr-004391
03:49:00.000 --> 03:49:01.700
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: that the Executive Secretary is former

asr-004392
03:49:01.700 --> 03:49:03.340
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Senate President Pro Tem.

asr-004392-split-2
03:49:03.340 --> 03:49:03.800
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Yes,

asr-004393
03:49:03.900 --> 03:49:05.940
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. President, that is absolutely correct.

asr-004394
03:49:06.440 --> 03:49:07.360
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: With that, Mr. President,

asr-004395
03:49:07.920 --> 03:49:10.220
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I move that the budgets of the President's

asr-004396
03:49:10.220 --> 03:49:11.720
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: offices under the OP

asr-004397
03:49:11.720 --> 03:49:13.640
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and President Management Staff

asr-004398
03:49:13.640 --> 03:49:15.420
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: be deemed submitted. I so move.

asr-004399
03:49:15.560 --> 03:49:17.580
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Any objection? Hearing none.

asr-004400
03:49:18.120 --> 03:49:19.620
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Deemed approved. Deemed submitted.

asr-004401
03:49:19.940 --> 03:49:21.960
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Thank you. May I ask for a minute's suspension, Mr. President?

asr-004402
03:49:22.060 --> 03:49:22.880
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Session suspended.

asr-004431
04:00:14.120 --> 04:00:15.420
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Thank you very much, Mr. President.

asr-004432
04:00:15.480 --> 04:00:21.220
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. President, I'm happy to announce that we'd like to move to take up the budget of the Department of Tourism.

asr-004433
04:00:22.580 --> 04:00:28.500
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: We'd like to hear the sponsor, Senator Erwin Tulfo, to provide details of the budget of the department.

asr-004434
04:00:28.500 --> 04:00:34.760
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Is there any objection? Hearing none, consideration of the budget of the Department of Tourism is in order.

asr-004435
04:00:35.380 --> 04:00:39.220
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We recognize the sponsor, Senator Erwin Tulfo.

asr-004436
04:00:39.480 --> 04:00:43.440
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Thank you, Mr. President. Thank you, Mr. Majority Floor Leader.

asr-004437
04:00:44.260 --> 04:00:51.160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: As Vice Chair of the Committee on Finance, I'm honored to defend the fiscal year 2027 budget of the Department of Tourism,

asr-004438
04:00:51.160 --> 04:00:57.100
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: its attached agencies, namely Intramuros Administration, National Parks Development Committee,

asr-004439
04:00:57.720 --> 04:00:58.480
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Philippine Commission

asr-004440
04:00:58.560 --> 04:01:03.820
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and Sports Scuba Diving and Corporations, namely the Duty-Free Philippines Corporation,

asr-004441
04:01:04.540 --> 04:01:09.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Tourism Infrastructure and Enterprise Zone Authority, and Tourism Promotions Board.

asr-004442
04:01:09.620 --> 04:01:16.120
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: At the core of the DOT's mandate is the unwavering commitment to position the Philippines as a premier,

asr-004443
04:01:16.700 --> 04:01:23.800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: sustainable, and inclusive tourist destination, ensuring the tourism sector remains a pillar of our national economy.

asr-004444
04:01:24.580 --> 04:01:27.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: In fiscal year 2025, the economic contribution of tourism,

asr-004445
04:01:28.500 --> 04:01:32.540
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: reached a staggering 2.27 trillion pesos.

asr-004446
04:01:33.240 --> 04:01:35.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Our tourist arrivals also continue to grow steadily,

asr-004447
04:01:36.280 --> 04:01:44.140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: from 3.31 million in the first semester of fiscal year 2025 to 3.41 million for fiscal year 2026.

asr-004448
04:01:44.700 --> 04:01:48.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: This growth is bolstered by DOT's outstanding global accomplishments,

asr-004449
04:01:48.400 --> 04:01:55.700
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: which include the successful launch of 20 new international flights as of September 2026,

asr-004450
04:01:56.220 --> 04:01:58.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: bringing in 472,240

asr-004451
04:01:58.500 --> 04:02:02.540
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: projected sold seats.

asr-004452
04:02:03.080 --> 04:02:09.160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Furthermore, the Philippines is proudly secured a spot as the number one retirement destination in the world.

asr-004453
04:02:09.280 --> 04:02:18.240
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Our unmatched marine biodiversity has also earned us the title of the world's leading dive destination for seven consecutive years,

asr-004454
04:02:18.840 --> 04:02:24.700
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: propelling us to the top five globally in terms of highest income generated from dive tourism.

asr-004455
04:02:25.700 --> 04:02:28.440
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Additionally, our aggressive push for astronomy tourism,

asr-004456
04:02:28.500 --> 04:02:30.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: has yielded remarkable results,

asr-004457
04:02:30.500 --> 04:02:35.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: generating a value of 366 million pesos in 2025.

asr-004458
04:02:35.500 --> 04:02:43.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Mr. President, despite these monumental achievements and the massive returns the sector brings to our economy,

asr-004459
04:02:43.500 --> 04:02:51.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: the funding for the department and its attached agencies will have a total available appropriation of only 4.03 billion

asr-004460
04:02:51.500 --> 04:02:54.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: in the National Expenditure Program of 2027.

asr-004461
04:02:54.500 --> 04:02:57.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: This is 337.7 million lower,

asr-004462
04:02:58.500 --> 04:03:07.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: presenting a 7.7% decrease compared to the 4.37 billion budget in 2026.

asr-004463
04:03:07.500 --> 04:03:09.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: As for the attached corporations,

asr-004464
04:03:09.500 --> 04:03:16.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: their respective funding levels show varying increases and reductions under the NEP 2027.

asr-004465
04:03:16.500 --> 04:03:27.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The duty-free Philippines corporation will have an increase in its total sources of funds from 2.074 billion in 2026 to 2.472 billion

asr-004466
04:03:27.500 --> 04:03:28.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: in 2027.

asr-004467
04:03:28.500 --> 04:03:30.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: On the other hand,

asr-004468
04:03:30.500 --> 04:03:41.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: TIEZA's approved corporate operating budget decreased from 12.7 billion in 2026 to 7.7 billion in 2027.

asr-004469
04:03:41.500 --> 04:03:52.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Similarly, the Tourism Promotions Board total funding declined from 1.864 billion in 2026 to 1.119 billion in 2027.

asr-004470
04:03:52.500 --> 04:03:57.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The National Parks Development Committee's COB also decreased

asr-004471
04:03:57.500 --> 04:04:02.460
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: From 81.6 million pesos to 73 million pesos.

asr-004472
04:04:03.040 --> 04:04:09.320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Meanwhile, the Philippine Retirement Authority will rely entirely on its corporate fund for 2027

asr-004473
04:04:09.320 --> 04:04:13.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: with no national government subsidy or trust receipts program.

asr-004474
04:04:14.720 --> 04:04:19.980
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We would like to thank the Chairperson of the Committee on Finance, Senator J.V. Ejercito,

asr-004475
04:04:20.280 --> 04:04:23.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: for his continued support strengthening the department's programs,

asr-004476
04:04:23.760 --> 04:04:29.480
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: particularly additional funding for marketing, promotions, branding of our tourism.

asr-004477
04:04:30.200 --> 04:04:33.800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Patuloy natin nawang mahalin at ipagmalaki ang ating bayan.

asr-004478
04:04:34.200 --> 04:04:36.240
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ika nga, love the Philippines.

asr-004479
04:04:36.900 --> 04:04:41.280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Mr. President, we are now open for questions and clarifications. Maraming salamat po.

asr-004480
04:04:41.840 --> 04:04:45.440
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you very much to the good sponsor, Senator Erwin Tulfo.

asr-004481
04:04:46.020 --> 04:04:52.660
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: To interpolate, we recognize our former Senate President, Senator Tito Soto.

asr-004482
04:04:53.760 --> 04:05:06.940
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you.

asr-004483
04:05:06.940 --> 04:05:08.460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you, Mr. President.

asr-004484
04:05:10.900 --> 04:05:14.700
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: You will have to forgive me. I will turn my back on you.

asr-004485
04:05:14.860 --> 04:05:20.120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I'm from old school. I usually still face the presiding officer.

asr-004486
04:05:20.320 --> 04:05:23.740
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: But because of the budget, we will have to...

asr-004487
04:05:23.900 --> 04:05:27.020
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-004488
04:05:27.200 --> 04:05:38.620
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: The Chairman, Chairman Erwin Tulfo, thank you very much for the very enlightening budget of the Department of Tourism.

asr-004489
04:05:39.280 --> 04:05:42.700
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: But I have a few questions for my clarification, if you don't mind.

asr-004490
04:05:43.900 --> 04:05:52.640
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: First, with the abolition of the travel tax already under the legislative process,

asr-004491
04:05:53.760 --> 04:05:56.700
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: how will this affect the mandate of Tiesa,

asr-004492
04:05:57.780 --> 04:06:05.520
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: particularly with regards to CHED's 40% share in the gross collection of travel tax?

asr-004493
04:06:06.160 --> 04:06:11.280
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: How massive is its effect as regards the free tertiary education?

asr-004494
04:06:16.580 --> 04:06:18.660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Actually, Mr. President, thank you.

asr-004495
04:06:19.940 --> 04:06:23.580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: At present, 50% of the travel tax is allocated to Tiesa.

asr-004496
04:06:23.760 --> 04:06:27.940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: For tourism development, 40% to CHED Tourism.

asr-004497
04:06:28.460 --> 04:06:31.320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Related educational programs, 10% to NCAA.

asr-004498
04:06:32.420 --> 04:06:34.320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: For the continuation of the support of the program,

asr-004499
04:06:34.500 --> 04:06:39.160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: the fund will be taken from GAA.

asr-004500
04:06:39.840 --> 04:06:47.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So, that's why the Department of Tourism, particularly the tourism, the Tiesa,

asr-004501
04:06:48.000 --> 04:06:49.820
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: is asking for a delay.

asr-004502
04:06:49.820 --> 04:06:52.820
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ika nga po dito, suspension muna of the...

asr-004503
04:06:53.760 --> 04:07:02.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: travel tax, replacing it with GAA appropriations.

asr-004504
04:07:02.300 --> 04:07:08.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Yun pong hinihingi ng Tiesa, kung maaari pong i-delay muna ang implementation nito, Mr. President.

asr-004505
04:07:11.220 --> 04:07:16.740
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Well, I am asking about the effect on the tertiary education

asr-004506
04:07:16.740 --> 04:07:21.840
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: because this also includes the medical scholarship program that we have.

asr-004507
04:07:23.060 --> 04:07:23.260
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: So,

asr-004508
04:07:23.760 --> 04:07:24.800
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: yeah, diba?

asr-004509
04:07:25.340 --> 04:07:27.040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Well, Mr. President,

asr-004510
04:07:27.420 --> 04:07:31.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: these are some of the effects of the abolition of the travel tax of the DOT

asr-004511
04:07:31.920 --> 04:07:34.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: that will affect the DOT's tourism program.

asr-004512
04:07:35.300 --> 04:07:35.880
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Number one,

asr-004513
04:07:36.740 --> 04:07:39.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: abolition would cut off the main funding source for DOT's

asr-004514
04:07:39.620 --> 04:07:41.700
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: tourism infrastructure program,

asr-004515
04:07:42.160 --> 04:07:43.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: which Tiesa implements.

asr-004516
04:07:43.600 --> 04:07:47.160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: About 91% of Tiesa's budget depends on travel tax.

asr-004517
04:07:48.060 --> 04:07:51.880
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Marami pong mga nagre-request as I go around doon na lang po sa probinsya namin,

asr-004518
04:07:51.880 --> 04:07:52.700
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: sa Mimaropa.

asr-004519
04:07:53.120 --> 04:07:53.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: A lot of,

asr-004520
04:07:53.760 --> 04:07:56.460
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: local government units are asking for assistance.

asr-004521
04:07:57.140 --> 04:07:59.360
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Yung mga tourist destinations po nila,

asr-004522
04:07:59.940 --> 04:08:02.220
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: sa Busuanga, sa Coron, sa El Nido,

asr-004523
04:08:02.840 --> 04:08:05.540
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: roads leading to tourist destinations,

asr-004524
04:08:06.080 --> 04:08:08.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: maapektuhan po yun, repairs of roads, bridges,

asr-004525
04:08:09.420 --> 04:08:11.220
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: definitely it will be affected.

asr-004526
04:08:12.420 --> 04:08:12.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Yun nga po,

asr-004527
04:08:12.900 --> 04:08:15.560
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: tourism infrastructure development all over the country,

asr-004528
04:08:16.300 --> 04:08:19.080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: designation development of tourism enterprise zones

asr-004529
04:08:19.080 --> 04:08:22.060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: that would attract investments in tourism,

asr-004530
04:08:22.060 --> 04:08:23.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: mga mababawasan po,

asr-004531
04:08:23.760 --> 04:08:26.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: rehabilitation and development tourism assets,

asr-004532
04:08:26.420 --> 04:08:29.520
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: development of resilient, sustainable tourism projects,

asr-004533
04:08:29.520 --> 04:08:33.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: such as sewerage treatment plants in Coron, El Nido, and Baguio,

asr-004534
04:08:33.760 --> 04:08:36.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and projects for seamless travel and tourism safety,

asr-004535
04:08:36.920 --> 04:08:39.520
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: such as rehabilitation of domestic projects.

asr-004536
04:08:39.520 --> 04:08:43.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: 2.95 billion din po mawawala sa CHED,

asr-004537
04:08:43.300 --> 04:08:46.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: 40,000 scholars po maapektuhan, Mr. President,

asr-004538
04:08:46.620 --> 04:08:50.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: ah, ah, Mr. ah, former Senate President.

asr-004539
04:08:50.760 --> 04:08:53.140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Would you know the status in the House of Representatives?

asr-004540
04:08:53.140 --> 04:08:55.120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Because as far as the Senate is concerned,

asr-004541
04:08:55.300 --> 04:08:57.560
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: we do not have a version yet.

asr-004542
04:08:58.220 --> 04:09:01.940
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: So, um, am I to take it that the Department of Tourism

asr-004543
04:09:01.940 --> 04:09:06.200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: is not in favor of this, uh, proposal?

asr-004544
04:09:06.840 --> 04:09:08.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Unfortunately, uh, Mr. President,

asr-004545
04:09:09.140 --> 04:09:12.120
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: uh, it has already passed in, uh, Congress.

asr-004546
04:09:13.220 --> 04:09:14.620
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: In the House of Representatives?

asr-004547
04:09:14.640 --> 04:09:15.600
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: In the committee level.

asr-004548
04:09:15.720 --> 04:09:18.140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Committee level only, but not, uh...

asr-004549
04:09:20.820 --> 04:09:23.120
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: House Bill 8464 has passed.

asr-004550
04:09:23.160 --> 04:09:28.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The third and final reading, uh, last March of 2026.

asr-004551
04:09:29.700 --> 04:09:33.040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The Senate, uh, the measure remains pending here

asr-004552
04:09:33.040 --> 04:09:35.880
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: in the Senate, uh, Mr. President.

asr-004553
04:09:36.420 --> 04:09:38.540
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Was the Department of Tourism heard

asr-004554
04:09:38.540 --> 04:09:42.080
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: in the hearings that were conducted in the House?

asr-004555
04:09:53.140 --> 04:09:58.800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Tiaza was, uh, invited several times, uh,

asr-004556
04:09:58.800 --> 04:10:02.700
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Mr. President, uh, uh, uh, former Senate President.

asr-004557
04:10:03.080 --> 04:10:09.320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Um, however, uh, the, the reasons were not clearly given to them.

asr-004558
04:10:09.320 --> 04:10:11.580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Why the abolition of the travel tax?

asr-004559
04:10:13.500 --> 04:10:14.320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Um...

asr-004560
04:10:14.320 --> 04:10:18.140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: This despite of, uh, their explanation, uh, Mr. President,

asr-004561
04:10:18.280 --> 04:10:23.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: na malaki po ang mawawala sa ikang, sa, sa Department of Tourism.

asr-004562
04:10:23.140 --> 04:10:25.440
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: At marami po mga apektohan, katulad po,

asr-004563
04:10:25.940 --> 04:10:30.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: nitong, uh, scholars po natin sa, uh, CHED.

asr-004564
04:10:31.320 --> 04:10:33.260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: And then yung mga infrastructure projects,

asr-004565
04:10:33.660 --> 04:10:37.660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: rehabilitation of infrastructure, uh, tourism, uh, areas.

asr-004566
04:10:38.140 --> 04:10:38.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Marami po mawawala.

asr-004567
04:10:39.100 --> 04:10:42.440
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Yet, despite all these explanations, uh, Mr. President,

asr-004568
04:10:42.900 --> 04:10:46.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: patuloy po at pumasa po ito sa, sa committee level ng Congress.

asr-004569
04:10:48.260 --> 04:10:51.140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Um, may I...

asr-004570
04:10:51.140 --> 04:10:53.120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: May I ask again?

asr-004571
04:10:53.140 --> 04:10:54.120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I, I, I forgot.

asr-004572
04:10:54.300 --> 04:10:57.420
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Who is the chairman of the Committee on Tourism here in the Senate, Mr. President?

asr-004573
04:11:04.600 --> 04:11:12.420
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The chairman of the, uh, Committee on Tourism is Senator Marco Leta, Your Honor.

asr-004574
04:11:13.780 --> 04:11:21.260
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: So, we would not know if, uh, the House version or the House bill has already been forwarded to the Senate Committee.

asr-004575
04:11:21.260 --> 04:11:22.980
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I believe this is, uh, under the...

asr-004576
04:11:22.980 --> 04:11:26.020
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Under the Committee on Ways and Means, uh...

asr-004577
04:11:26.020 --> 04:11:26.300
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ah.

asr-004578
04:11:27.460 --> 04:11:27.900
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Uh, Senator Soto.

asr-004579
04:11:27.900 --> 04:11:29.600
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Even in the House of Representatives, basically?

asr-004580
04:11:29.600 --> 04:11:31.500
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes, this is a taxation measure.

asr-004581
04:11:32.400 --> 04:11:32.600
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So...

asr-004582
04:11:32.600 --> 04:11:32.800
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-004583
04:11:32.960 --> 04:11:36.940
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, um, all taxation measures emanate from the House.

asr-004584
04:11:37.360 --> 04:11:41.160
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And I believe it's already referred in the Committee on Ways and Means here in the Senate.

asr-004585
04:11:41.160 --> 04:11:42.940
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And our Ways and Means is...

asr-004586
04:11:42.940 --> 04:11:44.020
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Senator Ping Lacson.

asr-004587
04:11:44.840 --> 04:11:46.020
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ah, Senator Ping Lacson.

asr-004588
04:11:46.120 --> 04:11:46.320
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Yes.

asr-004589
04:11:46.400 --> 04:11:46.800
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: All right.

asr-004590
04:11:47.840 --> 04:11:48.360
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Very good.

asr-004591
04:11:48.360 --> 04:11:52.360
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Uh, if I may add, Mr. President, um, uh,

asr-004592
04:11:52.980 --> 04:11:56.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: my, uh, distinguished, uh, colleague, uh,

asr-004593
04:11:56.300 --> 04:11:59.120
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: the Department of Tourism is hoping that the Senate

asr-004594
04:11:59.120 --> 04:12:04.200
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: may reconsider the transition period requested by Tiaza at this point.

asr-004595
04:12:04.280 --> 04:12:05.400
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: If ever we do agree.

asr-004596
04:12:06.300 --> 04:12:06.740
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Exactly.

asr-004597
04:12:07.020 --> 04:12:09.020
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: That there'll be a transition period.

asr-004598
04:12:09.760 --> 04:12:10.720
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Just in case.

asr-004599
04:12:10.940 --> 04:12:11.680
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Anyway, thank you.

asr-004600
04:12:12.240 --> 04:12:13.160
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Moving forward.

asr-004601
04:12:14.060 --> 04:12:19.100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: May I know the plans of the Department on boosting domestic tourism

asr-004602
04:12:19.100 --> 04:12:22.500
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: given that, uh, traveling to our neighboring countries,

asr-004603
04:12:22.980 --> 04:12:27.640
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: now, is cheaper than traveling to tourist destinations in the Philippines?

asr-004604
04:12:28.820 --> 04:12:29.720
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: But this is local.

asr-004605
04:12:36.300 --> 04:12:39.480
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Well, uh, Mr. President, um,

asr-004606
04:12:39.820 --> 04:12:43.460
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: the DDOT is coordinating right now with 18 regional offices,

asr-004607
04:12:43.460 --> 04:12:47.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: uh, which work closely with LGUs and provide technical assistance

asr-004608
04:12:47.420 --> 04:12:50.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: in developing and improving local tourism destinations.

asr-004609
04:12:51.440 --> 04:12:52.940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Priority areas, uh,

asr-004610
04:12:52.940 --> 04:12:54.260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: with existing airports.

asr-004611
04:12:54.820 --> 04:12:56.380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Problem po kasi, Mr. President,

asr-004612
04:12:56.560 --> 04:12:57.800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: ay yung ating pong airports.

asr-004613
04:12:58.520 --> 04:13:00.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Uh, like, like Siargao,

asr-004614
04:13:00.840 --> 04:13:03.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: strengthen their airport capacity and international connectivity.

asr-004615
04:13:03.900 --> 04:13:07.960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: You have Coron, maximize the existing airport to support

asr-004616
04:13:07.960 --> 04:13:10.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: increased island, marine, and dive tourism.

asr-004617
04:13:10.960 --> 04:13:11.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: El Nido also.

asr-004618
04:13:12.580 --> 04:13:16.000
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Build an existing airport and further develop public-private partnership.

asr-004619
04:13:16.440 --> 04:13:17.980
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: San Vicente also in Palawan.

asr-004620
04:13:18.420 --> 04:13:21.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Siquijor in the Visayas, strengthen airport connectivity.

asr-004621
04:13:21.860 --> 04:13:22.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: These are, uh,

asr-004622
04:13:22.940 --> 04:13:25.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: uh, uh, the efforts are being done by, uh,

asr-004623
04:13:26.020 --> 04:13:27.000
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: the DDOT right now.

asr-004624
04:13:27.060 --> 04:13:29.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: In coordination, definitely, of course,

asr-004625
04:13:29.240 --> 04:13:30.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: with the Department of Transportation.

asr-004626
04:13:31.360 --> 04:13:33.900
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Well, aside from the issue of transportation,

asr-004627
04:13:34.200 --> 04:13:36.300
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: uh, Your Honor, uh, Mr. President,

asr-004628
04:13:37.440 --> 04:13:38.000
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: um,

asr-004629
04:13:39.540 --> 04:13:44.260
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: are we not pricing our domestic tourists

asr-004630
04:13:44.260 --> 04:13:47.280
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: out of, uh, vacationing in our country?

asr-004631
04:13:47.400 --> 04:13:50.580
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: By a few months ago, I, I read some articles,

asr-004632
04:13:50.740 --> 04:13:52.320
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: and that's why I bring this up.

asr-004633
04:13:52.940 --> 04:13:55.660
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: There was an article released stating that a

asr-004634
04:13:55.660 --> 04:13:58.460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Pampano dish in Panglao Bohol

asr-004635
04:13:58.460 --> 04:14:01.560
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: costs 1,650.

asr-004636
04:14:01.560 --> 04:14:05.560
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: A grab car in Vietnam, uh,

asr-004637
04:14:06.400 --> 04:14:09.500
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: costs around 80 pesos to get around

asr-004638
04:14:09.500 --> 04:14:11.900
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: the old quarter of Hanoi.

asr-004639
04:14:11.980 --> 04:14:14.240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: While again, in Panglao Bohol, it costs, uh,

asr-004640
04:14:14.240 --> 04:14:18.600
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: 100 to 250 pesos for a tricycle ride around Panglao itself.

asr-004641
04:14:19.600 --> 04:14:22.920
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Um, this, um, uh, this was, uh,

asr-004642
04:14:22.940 --> 04:14:25.120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: written out, uh,

asr-004643
04:14:25.520 --> 04:14:27.980
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I, I, I've read this somewhere in the, in the newspapers.

asr-004644
04:14:28.600 --> 04:14:32.440
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: It does seem that we're pricing our domestic tourists

asr-004645
04:14:32.440 --> 04:14:35.260
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: out of exploring our beautiful country.

asr-004646
04:14:35.260 --> 04:14:38.860
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: What can we, what can the Department of Tourism do about this?

asr-004647
04:14:39.340 --> 04:14:40.860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Specifically, Mr. President,

asr-004648
04:14:41.140 --> 04:14:44.240
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: particularly the, uh, issue, uh,

asr-004649
04:14:44.260 --> 04:14:46.100
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: over tourism in Bohol right now,

asr-004650
04:14:46.660 --> 04:14:49.060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: well, the, the DOT, um,

asr-004651
04:14:49.500 --> 04:14:52.660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: is coordinating with the LGU to monitor prices of goods.

asr-004652
04:14:52.940 --> 04:14:54.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: And restaurants in Panglao.

asr-004653
04:14:55.360 --> 04:14:57.960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: To complement this, the Panglao price monitoring team

asr-004654
04:14:57.960 --> 04:15:00.040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: intends to conduct thorough monitoring.

asr-004655
04:15:00.000 --> 04:15:12.280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: During the meeting of the Presidential Assistant for Visayas, it was decided the Department of Trade and Industry would be responsible for the regulation and monitoring of goods services.

asr-004656
04:15:13.040 --> 04:15:18.860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The DOT, however, commenced to refer reported incidents of overpricing to DTI-7 for proper handling.

asr-004657
04:15:18.860 --> 04:15:29.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: In short, Mr. President, dapat po kasama po ang ibang mga ahensya na tumutulong sa Department of Tourism to monitor, not only po other agencies like DTI.

asr-004658
04:15:30.000 --> 04:15:32.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: But also the local government units para ma-monitor.

asr-004659
04:15:32.840 --> 04:15:42.080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Because DOT doesn't have enough ikang personal to monitor all these prices in the market, yung fare ng mga local transportation.

asr-004660
04:15:42.080 --> 04:15:47.720
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: There has to be help from other agencies as well, Mr. President.

asr-004661
04:15:49.720 --> 04:15:54.580
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you for that. But sometime ago, I distinctly remember.

asr-004662
04:15:59.060 --> 04:15:59.980
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: We said,

asr-004663
04:16:00.000 --> 04:16:04.100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: We should give more concentration to the Department itself.

asr-004664
04:16:06.140 --> 04:16:11.820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I believe that the number one dollar earner of the Philippines should be tourism.

asr-004665
04:16:13.560 --> 04:16:15.220
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: It is possible.

asr-004666
04:16:16.840 --> 04:16:22.640
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The Department of Tourism agrees with the former Senate President, definitely.

asr-004667
04:16:22.640 --> 04:16:25.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Pero there's a lot of factors po kasi daw.

asr-004668
04:16:26.340 --> 04:16:29.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The problem with our low tourism.

asr-004669
04:16:30.000 --> 04:16:31.140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Arrivals.

asr-004670
04:16:31.140 --> 04:16:38.860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: One of those, even local tourism, Mr. President, the problem is yung pong transportation.

asr-004671
04:16:40.100 --> 04:16:50.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: If you go to small islands in the Visayas and in Luzon, before reaching that area, you have to travel to Clark, Pampanga.

asr-004672
04:16:50.860 --> 04:16:52.880
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The problem kasi it was already transferred.

asr-004673
04:16:53.040 --> 04:16:58.340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Pag naka-turbo prop yung aeroplano, because the airport in the destination that you're going small,

asr-004674
04:16:58.340 --> 04:16:59.340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: you have to...

asr-004675
04:17:00.000 --> 04:17:04.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Turbo props are now flying out from Clark and not anymore in Naia.

asr-004676
04:17:05.260 --> 04:17:06.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Nilipat na po ng NMIC.

asr-004677
04:17:06.920 --> 04:17:18.720
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So yung mga tao na instead of going to, for example, ng Siquijor, because turbo prop po yung twin engine na LEC or Coron, Palawan,

asr-004678
04:17:19.240 --> 04:17:28.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: medyo tinatamad na, Mr. President, na pumunta pa sa Clark para makapunta lang sa Coron,

asr-004679
04:17:28.300 --> 04:17:30.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: dahil nga po dun lumayo.

asr-004680
04:17:31.320 --> 04:17:32.320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So nabawasan po.

asr-004681
04:17:32.480 --> 04:17:34.860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The Department of Tourism noticed this.

asr-004682
04:17:35.220 --> 04:17:40.380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Noong magkaroon po ng paglilipat ng ika nga naka-turbo prop na aeroplano,

asr-004683
04:17:40.780 --> 04:17:46.060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: maliliit na airplanes that they use para po sa mga island na mga destinations natin.

asr-004684
04:17:46.180 --> 04:17:48.580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So people, Mr. President, are tired.

asr-004685
04:17:48.940 --> 04:17:52.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So instead of going to local destinations, halos pareho lang naman ang presyo,

asr-004686
04:17:52.920 --> 04:17:57.640
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: they'd rather go overseas, they'd rather go to Thailand to go there.

asr-004687
04:17:57.640 --> 04:17:59.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Or Vietnam, which is more cheaper.

asr-004688
04:18:00.300 --> 04:18:01.560
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So yun po ang nagiging problem.

asr-004689
04:18:01.740 --> 04:18:09.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kaya nga po, we have already, in one of the hearings, I've already asked the DOTR to look into this.

asr-004690
04:18:09.780 --> 04:18:10.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Paano pwedeng gawin?

asr-004691
04:18:10.920 --> 04:18:13.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kasi tinatamad po yung mga kababayan natin.

asr-004692
04:18:13.400 --> 04:18:16.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Instead of going to Clark, mapapatagal po ang biyahe nila,

asr-004693
04:18:17.360 --> 04:18:19.480
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: e pupunta na lang po sa ibang bansa at mas mura pa.

asr-004694
04:18:19.480 --> 04:18:25.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Another issue, Mr. President, is yung cost po ng fair ng aeroplano.

asr-004695
04:18:26.220 --> 04:18:27.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ang sagot po kasi dyan,

asr-004696
04:18:27.640 --> 04:18:29.720
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: mga airline industries,

asr-004697
04:18:30.400 --> 04:18:34.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: sinasagot na po kasi ng pasahero dahil hindi po napupuno.

asr-004698
04:18:34.460 --> 04:18:38.040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Like if you're going, kaya nga po may mga areas tayo dito sa Pilipinas,

asr-004699
04:18:38.560 --> 04:18:42.280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: like in my Maropa, in my area, in my region,

asr-004700
04:18:42.820 --> 04:18:45.820
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: may mga flights po dati dyan sa Marinduque,

asr-004701
04:18:45.920 --> 04:18:47.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: may mga flights po dati dyan sa Rumblon,

asr-004702
04:18:48.420 --> 04:18:50.320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: naputol na po because it's so expensive,

asr-004703
04:18:50.320 --> 04:18:52.160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: hindi po napupuno yung flights.

asr-004704
04:18:52.740 --> 04:18:56.560
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Parang pinagbabayad po yung isang pasahero, round trip ka agad.

asr-004705
04:18:56.880 --> 04:18:57.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So para pagbalik,

asr-004706
04:18:57.680 --> 04:18:59.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: ng aeroplano, parang may sakay na pasahero.

asr-004707
04:18:59.680 --> 04:19:03.040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So the fees are so exorbitant, masyadong malaki.

asr-004708
04:19:03.040 --> 04:19:11.580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kaya this turns off yung mga would-be local tourists in several local destinations, Mr. President.

asr-004709
04:19:11.620 --> 04:19:17.420
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: So, well, then we expect the department to reason to find solutions

asr-004710
04:19:17.420 --> 04:19:26.180
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: and suggest solutions to the executive department when it comes to these issues, hopefully.

asr-004711
04:19:26.180 --> 04:19:26.280
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Hopefully.

asr-004712
04:19:27.640 --> 04:19:33.680
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Mr. President, actually, there's an ongoing dialogue with the Department of Tourism

asr-004713
04:19:33.680 --> 04:19:36.080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and the Department of Transportation regarding this matter.

asr-004714
04:19:36.600 --> 04:19:41.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Pero when it comes po dun sa airline, kailangan din po isama ang NMIC

asr-004715
04:19:41.500 --> 04:19:44.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: because sila po yung may control, sila po yung may instruction.

asr-004716
04:19:44.920 --> 04:19:51.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Naalisin na po yung mga turboprop airplanes going to small island tourist destination.

asr-004717
04:19:51.560 --> 04:19:52.980
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Inilipat na po nila sa Clark.

asr-004718
04:19:53.060 --> 04:19:53.940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So that is the problem.

asr-004719
04:19:54.360 --> 04:19:57.580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: People are getting tired traveling to Clark.

asr-004720
04:19:57.580 --> 04:20:02.960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: For another hour, then when they come home, they have to travel again another hour going back to Metro Manila.

asr-004721
04:20:03.360 --> 04:20:05.660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kaya po doon nakita na may problema ho dito.

asr-004722
04:20:05.880 --> 04:20:06.320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ika nga.

asr-004723
04:20:06.820 --> 04:20:11.200
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Because yung travel time, it's so expensive.

asr-004724
04:20:12.360 --> 04:20:16.440
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: But there is a coordination between the DOT and the DOTR.

asr-004725
04:20:16.740 --> 04:20:18.240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Alright. We will look forward to that.

asr-004726
04:20:18.660 --> 04:20:19.220
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you.

asr-004727
04:20:20.120 --> 04:20:21.240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Let me move on.

asr-004728
04:20:21.240 --> 04:20:27.240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: One of the best ways to teach history and share the...

asr-004729
04:20:27.580 --> 04:20:31.980
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: The beautiful culture of the Philippines is through tourism.

asr-004730
04:20:32.740 --> 04:20:39.720
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Would you have any plans to put up more museums and other interactive displays

asr-004731
04:20:39.720 --> 04:20:42.780
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: in our top tourism destinations for this purpose?

asr-004732
04:20:44.720 --> 04:20:49.220
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And would it be included in your budget for 2027?

asr-004733
04:20:57.580 --> 04:21:18.340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: If the president is asking if there's a plan to set up more museums,

asr-004734
04:21:18.340 --> 04:21:24.340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: unfortunately, there is none right now, Mr. President, because of budget constraints.

asr-004735
04:21:24.580 --> 04:21:27.340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Pero what DOT is doing is upgrading training programs.

asr-004736
04:21:27.580 --> 04:21:33.960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: For tour guides, another thing, cultural heritage destinations, pinapalakas po yun.

asr-004737
04:21:34.360 --> 04:21:40.960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Like in archaeological sites, museums, world heritage, treasuries, cultural properties, etc.

asr-004738
04:21:41.700 --> 04:21:43.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Then creative tourism, new generation tourism,

asr-004739
04:21:44.000 --> 04:21:49.140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: that places an emphasis on engaging tourists with local culture, arts, and heritage, Mr. President.

asr-004740
04:21:50.160 --> 04:21:55.660
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I hope the department tries to develop the idea.

asr-004741
04:21:55.660 --> 04:21:56.660
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I think it's a very...

asr-004742
04:21:57.580 --> 04:22:04.000
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Well, to include also, Mr. President, we still have the Nayang Pilipino right now.

asr-004743
04:22:04.000 --> 04:22:13.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Total open space and museum visitors was listed at 11,165 as of October 2026, Mr. President.

asr-004744
04:22:16.020 --> 04:22:16.900
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Okay.

asr-004745
04:22:18.480 --> 04:22:22.020
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Again, I move forward.

asr-004746
04:22:23.200 --> 04:22:26.820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: For the National Parks Development Committee,

asr-004747
04:22:26.820 --> 04:22:34.820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: it's very obvious that there are lesser public parks in the metros for children to play

asr-004748
04:22:34.820 --> 04:22:40.340
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: and for families to just lounge around for free.

asr-004749
04:22:40.840 --> 04:22:44.000
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: In fact, we have more malls than parks.

asr-004750
04:22:45.580 --> 04:22:51.220
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Do we have plans of acquiring lots and creating free parks and conducive open spaces?

asr-004751
04:22:52.020 --> 04:22:55.200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Whether Metro Manila or other parts of the country,

asr-004752
04:22:55.200 --> 04:22:56.200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: because the LGUs may...

asr-004753
04:22:56.820 --> 04:23:01.780
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: may be harnessed to support this move by the department.

asr-004754
04:23:01.780 --> 04:23:11.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: As much as they would love to focus on developing more parks, Mr. President,

asr-004755
04:23:11.700 --> 04:23:16.540
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: unfortunately, the funding gaps for park development is down to 65 million,

asr-004756
04:23:16.940 --> 04:23:21.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: or they needed 65 million to complete the Japanese Garden Redevelopment Landscape Utilities.

asr-004757
04:23:22.820 --> 04:23:26.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: For fiscal year 2027 budget, reductions may affect priority programs,

asr-004758
04:23:26.820 --> 04:23:27.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and capital outlay.

asr-004759
04:23:28.540 --> 04:23:31.200
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: National Parks Development Committee,

asr-004760
04:23:31.880 --> 04:23:35.260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: in their GAA last year, 2026,

asr-004761
04:23:35.600 --> 04:23:38.000
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: it was like 316.8 million.

asr-004762
04:23:38.640 --> 04:23:41.860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Pero in the NEP of 2027, it's down to 286.

asr-004763
04:23:42.180 --> 04:23:46.260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Well, we will try, the Senate will try to maintain that at 286.

asr-004764
04:23:46.920 --> 04:23:50.820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And also, can't you try to...

asr-004765
04:23:50.820 --> 04:23:55.240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: can't the department try to coordinate with local government units?

asr-004766
04:23:55.240 --> 04:23:55.300
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Yes.

asr-004767
04:23:56.820 --> 04:23:58.540
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Because the LGUs may have a lot of ideas.

asr-004768
04:23:59.140 --> 04:24:06.420
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Maybe by coordinating with them, helping the tourism department,

asr-004769
04:24:06.860 --> 04:24:07.880
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: maybe there are things like that.

asr-004770
04:24:08.040 --> 04:24:13.040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Just bringing up the idea, Your Honor, Mr. President.

asr-004771
04:24:15.500 --> 04:24:19.060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Unfortunately, according to the DOT, Mr. President,

asr-004772
04:24:19.740 --> 04:24:26.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: there is no funding yet for such activity or programs.

asr-004773
04:24:26.820 --> 04:24:28.080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: As of yet.

asr-004774
04:24:28.580 --> 04:24:36.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So, it's very hard for them to look for, to develop parks in different parts of our country.

asr-004775
04:24:38.200 --> 04:24:44.820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Well, as I said, baka pwedeng in coordination with some LGUs na maluluwag pa.

asr-004776
04:24:45.340 --> 04:24:55.200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Anyway, again, I throw the idea to the department for their consideration.

asr-004777
04:24:55.700 --> 04:24:56.500
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: No.

asr-004778
04:24:56.820 --> 04:25:03.300
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I heard you earlier mention figures about international tourists.

asr-004779
04:25:03.880 --> 04:25:09.600
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: In 2015, and this is based on the old records that I have now, so correct me if I'm wrong,

asr-004780
04:25:10.660 --> 04:25:14.040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: we had roughly 5.3 million international tourists.

asr-004781
04:25:14.920 --> 04:25:18.920
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: For reference, Vietnam had around 7.9 million.

asr-004782
04:25:18.920 --> 04:25:26.300
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: So now, in 2025, 10 years after, we have 6.8 million.

asr-004783
04:25:26.440 --> 04:25:26.800
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Is that correct?

asr-004784
04:25:26.820 --> 04:25:34.560
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: But Vietnam has now 21.2 million international tourists.

asr-004785
04:25:35.560 --> 04:25:45.260
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: My question is, why in the past decade, our tourism generally could be said as static?

asr-004786
04:25:47.980 --> 04:25:50.900
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Parang maliit yung itinaas natin.

asr-004787
04:25:51.440 --> 04:25:53.060
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ngunit sila ay napakalaki.

asr-004788
04:25:53.160 --> 04:25:53.940
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ano bang nangyari?

asr-004789
04:25:54.060 --> 04:25:54.820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ano bang diferensya?

asr-004790
04:25:54.820 --> 04:25:55.240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ano ba?

asr-004791
04:25:56.820 --> 04:25:59.140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ano mga malaking pag-uulang natin?

asr-004792
04:26:08.780 --> 04:26:10.120
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Alright, Mr. President.

asr-004793
04:26:10.400 --> 04:26:16.380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The explanation of the Department of Tourism, the reason why our country is lagging behind in tourist arrivals,

asr-004794
04:26:16.380 --> 04:26:24.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: our neighbors, Thailand, Malaysia, and Vietnam, have been investing big amounts for tourism.

asr-004795
04:26:25.460 --> 04:26:26.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: While tayo po,

asr-004796
04:26:26.400 --> 04:26:28.660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: compared to those countries,

asr-004797
04:26:29.240 --> 04:26:32.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: is only like about one-fourth of how much they spend.

asr-004798
04:26:34.260 --> 04:26:36.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: I'll give you some figures, Mr. President.

asr-004799
04:26:36.420 --> 04:26:46.260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: For example, the budget of Thailand for tourism in 2024 is $167.9 million.

asr-004800
04:26:46.920 --> 04:26:47.660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: This is in dollars.

asr-004801
04:26:48.220 --> 04:26:50.940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Malaysia at $262.87 million.

asr-004802
04:26:51.500 --> 04:26:53.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Vietnam at $147.92.

asr-004803
04:26:54.520 --> 04:26:56.380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Singapore at $431.2.

asr-004804
04:26:56.400 --> 04:27:00.140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Indonesia at $34.36 million.

asr-004805
04:27:00.760 --> 04:27:03.380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Philippines is just $52.1 million.

asr-004806
04:27:04.180 --> 04:27:07.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So, ang arrival po, makikita din, that will translate.

asr-004807
04:27:08.220 --> 04:27:18.280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The Thailand expenditure on the tourism brought them around 35.55 million tourists in 2024.

asr-004808
04:27:18.480 --> 04:27:21.040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Malaysia, $25.02 million.

asr-004809
04:27:21.540 --> 04:27:23.800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Vietnam, $17.58 million.

asr-004810
04:27:24.020 --> 04:27:25.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Singapore, $16 million.

asr-004811
04:27:25.180 --> 04:27:26.240
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Indonesia, $17.58 million.

asr-004812
04:27:26.240 --> 04:27:27.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Malaysia, $13.89 million.

asr-004813
04:27:28.480 --> 04:27:33.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: And because of our funding, we only got 5.95 million tourists, Mr. President.

asr-004814
04:27:36.920 --> 04:27:38.040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: So, poonan.

asr-004815
04:27:38.900 --> 04:27:39.460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Poonan.

asr-004816
04:27:40.100 --> 04:27:43.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The problem really, it's a fact, Mr. President.

asr-004817
04:27:43.600 --> 04:27:46.060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So, that's where we're having problems right now.

asr-004818
04:27:46.340 --> 04:27:48.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Even in advertisements, Mr. President,

asr-004819
04:27:48.640 --> 04:27:52.940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: if you notice other countries like Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand,

asr-004820
04:27:52.940 --> 04:27:55.640
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: you will see them in international news.

asr-004821
04:27:56.240 --> 04:27:58.680
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: CNN, BBC, Fox News.

asr-004822
04:27:59.000 --> 04:28:04.660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: They advertise major newspapers, New York Times, etc., Singapore's Three Times.

asr-004823
04:28:05.040 --> 04:28:05.520
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: They are there.

asr-004824
04:28:06.180 --> 04:28:10.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Unfortunately, because of a limited budget, we cannot afford.

asr-004825
04:28:10.560 --> 04:28:13.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We did that a couple of years ago in the buses of England,

asr-004826
04:28:13.900 --> 04:28:21.980
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: but that's not enough to boost, to advertise our tourism in the Philippines, Mr. President.

asr-004827
04:28:22.900 --> 04:28:26.000
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Well, thank you for your answers.

asr-004828
04:28:26.240 --> 04:28:27.760
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And thank you to the department.

asr-004829
04:28:28.080 --> 04:28:34.980
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: But, well, I hope we could get back to the drawing board.

asr-004830
04:28:36.080 --> 04:28:37.060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Let me add to that.

asr-004831
04:28:37.060 --> 04:28:43.040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And study the possibilities of these suggestions that might be able to develop.

asr-004832
04:28:43.660 --> 04:28:46.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Another thing, Mr. President, is like,

asr-004833
04:28:47.580 --> 04:28:53.100
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: I myself would suggest to the DOT to stick with one branding campaign.

asr-004834
04:28:53.100 --> 04:28:56.040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Because we noticed the change of administration.

asr-004835
04:28:56.240 --> 04:29:01.360
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Before, it's like, now it's love the Philippines.

asr-004836
04:29:01.620 --> 04:29:08.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Before, it was like, wow, Philippines during the time of former Senator Gordon.

asr-004837
04:29:08.540 --> 04:29:13.200
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: And then, it's more fun in the Philippines.

asr-004838
04:29:13.780 --> 04:29:14.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Wala siyang identity.

asr-004839
04:29:14.980 --> 04:29:16.220
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We don't have an identity.

asr-004840
04:29:16.760 --> 04:29:19.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Unlike Malaysia, Mr. President, if you notice in the commercials,

asr-004841
04:29:20.320 --> 04:29:22.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: they've been using this for the past 20 years.

asr-004842
04:29:23.480 --> 04:29:24.940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Malaysia, truly Asia.

asr-004843
04:29:25.360 --> 04:29:26.160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Tayo,

asr-004845
04:29:26.440 --> 04:29:29.000
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: nakailang palit na ho tayo for the past 20 years.

asr-004846
04:29:29.380 --> 04:29:31.040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So, I guess we have to stick to that brand.

asr-004847
04:29:31.160 --> 04:29:32.460
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: para tatatak po sa isipan,

asr-004848
04:29:33.100 --> 04:29:34.080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: magkakaroon ng recall.

asr-004849
04:29:35.820 --> 04:29:37.060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Philippines should be there.

asr-004850
04:29:37.140 --> 04:29:37.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Love the Philippines.

asr-004851
04:29:38.040 --> 04:29:40.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: And then, let's stick with love the Philippines

asr-004852
04:29:40.020 --> 04:29:43.080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: so that it will stick to the minds of the viewers and listeners

asr-004853
04:29:43.080 --> 04:29:46.160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: listening to the advertisements of the DOT.

asr-004854
04:29:46.460 --> 04:29:46.880
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Mr. President.

asr-004855
04:29:48.800 --> 04:29:51.920
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Just to end my interpellation, Your Honor,

asr-004856
04:29:52.080 --> 04:29:55.460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I have a suggestion that you should study that.

asr-004857
04:29:55.460 --> 04:29:57.760
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Tutal, meron tayong mga pinag-usapan na ganyan.

asr-004858
04:29:58.180 --> 04:29:59.100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Pero ito, ibang klase.

asr-004859
04:30:00.000 --> 04:30:06.540
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Many years ago, during the younger days of myself and Senator Aimee Marcos,

asr-004860
04:30:07.960 --> 04:30:10.520
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Hawaii was not that popular.

asr-004861
04:30:11.640 --> 04:30:13.140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Diba? It was not that popular.

asr-004862
04:30:13.580 --> 04:30:15.860
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: You know what the Department of Tourism of Hawaii did?

asr-004863
04:30:16.360 --> 04:30:19.360
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: They created a TV show entitled Hawaii Five-O.

asr-004864
04:30:20.460 --> 04:30:25.580
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: All of a sudden, Hawaii was in the limelight all over the world.

asr-004865
04:30:25.580 --> 04:30:34.500
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And perhaps the Department of Tourism can study something like that for, let's say, Boracay or somewhere up north.

asr-004866
04:30:36.380 --> 04:30:38.540
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Or the islands up north.

asr-004867
04:30:39.060 --> 04:30:39.780
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Maraming maganda.

asr-004868
04:30:40.340 --> 04:30:40.980
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Isabela.

asr-004869
04:30:41.840 --> 04:30:42.040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Diba?

asr-004870
04:30:42.220 --> 04:30:43.380
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And all those places.

asr-004871
04:30:43.520 --> 04:30:43.660
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Baka.

asr-004872
04:30:45.080 --> 04:30:49.160
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: It's a matter of promo.

asr-004873
04:30:50.120 --> 04:30:50.540
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Promo.

