asr-006276
05:17:59.180 --> 05:18:00.080
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Mark Villars, recognize.

asr-006277
05:18:04.180 --> 05:18:07.120
Senator Mark A. Villar: Good evening.

asr-006278
05:18:08.260 --> 05:18:13.680
Senator Mark A. Villar: I just wanted to continue a line of questioning that was started yesterday

asr-006279
05:18:13.680 --> 05:18:21.280
Senator Mark A. Villar: when I was interviewing the DBM about their recent numbers regarding to the GDP.

asr-006280
05:18:21.280 --> 05:18:28.600
Senator Mark A. Villar: And I mentioned that tourism is one of the main drivers of GDP growth in many other countries.

asr-006281
05:18:29.180 --> 05:18:33.560
Senator Mark A. Villar: Some examples include Thailand, even Vietnam now.

asr-006282
05:18:33.700 --> 05:18:35.100
Senator Mark A. Villar: They're very aggressive with tourism.

asr-006283
05:18:36.080 --> 05:18:41.380
Senator Mark A. Villar: And I mentioned yesterday that in order for us to maximize our tourism,

asr-006284
05:18:41.660 --> 05:18:45.440
Senator Mark A. Villar: it has to be a comprehensive effort from all of government.

asr-006285
05:18:46.460 --> 05:18:49.220
Senator Mark A. Villar: It has to include multiple agencies.

asr-006286
05:18:49.220 --> 05:18:55.220
Senator Mark A. Villar: You can't just point to one thing and say that if we improve this, tourism will rebound.

asr-006287
05:18:56.420 --> 05:18:58.220
Senator Mark A. Villar: It has to be infrastructure.

asr-006288
05:18:58.540 --> 05:18:59.140
Senator Mark A. Villar: It has to be market.

asr-006289
05:18:59.180 --> 05:18:59.560
Senator Mark A. Villar: It has to be marketing.

asr-006290
05:18:59.800 --> 05:19:00.700
Senator Mark A. Villar: It has to be policy.

asr-006291
05:19:00.860 --> 05:19:02.060
Senator Mark A. Villar: It has to be even incentives.

asr-006292
05:19:02.840 --> 05:19:07.840
Senator Mark A. Villar: So my question is, what are the steps that the DOT is taking now

asr-006293
05:19:07.840 --> 05:19:17.500
Senator Mark A. Villar: to coordinate all the agencies and work together so that we can have a comprehensive tourism strategy?

asr-006294
05:19:18.060 --> 05:19:20.580
Senator Mark A. Villar: And perhaps if there is a tourism strategy, what is that?

asr-006295
05:19:22.760 --> 05:19:27.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: To start with, Mr. President, let's talk about local tourism first.

asr-006296
05:19:27.780 --> 05:19:29.080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: First, there was really...

asr-006297
05:19:29.180 --> 05:19:35.520
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: There was really a drop in tourism arrivals in various local tourist destinations

asr-006298
05:19:35.520 --> 05:19:44.220
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: because of the fact of moving out of turboprop airplanes from Naia to Clark, Pampanga.

asr-006299
05:19:44.960 --> 05:19:47.720
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Medyo tinatamad po na yung mga kababayan natin.

asr-006300
05:19:47.900 --> 05:19:49.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Napupunta lang po sila sa Batanes.

asr-006301
05:19:50.340 --> 05:19:52.200
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: That's just about a 30-minute ride.

asr-006302
05:19:52.580 --> 05:19:54.480
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Iaabutin po ng two hours and a half.

asr-006303
05:19:54.480 --> 05:19:58.480
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: In my province alone, in Coron, the flight is just about...

asr-006304
05:19:59.180 --> 05:20:00.100
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: 40 minutes from Naia.

asr-006305
05:20:00.580 --> 05:20:02.860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Now it will take them about two hours and a half

asr-006306
05:20:02.860 --> 05:20:04.440
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: because two hours going to Clark

asr-006307
05:20:04.440 --> 05:20:08.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and then yung flight pa na 40 minutes, about two hours and 40.

asr-006308
05:20:08.700 --> 05:20:11.480
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So dito pa lamang po, because they moved it,

asr-006309
05:20:11.820 --> 05:20:13.240
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: tinatamad na po yung mga kababayan.

asr-006310
05:20:13.380 --> 05:20:18.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kaya there was really a significant drop in tourist arrivals sa mga local destinations.

asr-006311
05:20:19.100 --> 05:20:25.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Now, pertaining to the tourist arrivals like foreigners, Mr. President,

asr-006312
05:20:25.900 --> 05:20:29.140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: the problem here is yung advertisements natin.

asr-006313
05:20:29.180 --> 05:20:38.820
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We're in several countries have been spending several millions, Mr. President.

asr-006338
05:20:58.580 --> 05:21:02.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: There's a glaring difference, Mr. President,

asr-006339
05:21:02.020 --> 05:21:03.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: on how much each country,

asr-006340
05:21:03.760 --> 05:21:08.320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: If we compare ourselves to Vietnam, Singapore, Thailand.

asr-006341
05:21:08.880 --> 05:21:12.140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: They spend like over hundreds of millions of dollars,

asr-006342
05:21:12.580 --> 05:21:17.200
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: while the Philippines only spends like around 52 million dollars.

asr-006343
05:21:17.200 --> 05:21:19.960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So, you see the disparity Mr.President.

asr-006344
05:21:20.140 --> 05:21:22.240
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Dahil sa napaka laki.

asr-006345
05:21:22.960 --> 05:21:24.540
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: I'll give you, I'll start your example.

asr-006346
05:21:24.960 --> 05:21:28.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: In 2025 lamang po,

asr-006347
05:21:28.500 --> 05:21:40.280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Thailand spent $196 million and yung arrival po nila was 32.97 million tourists.

asr-006348
05:21:40.740 --> 05:21:47.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Malaysia spent $335 million, dumating po sa kanila is 26.61 million tourists.

asr-006349
05:21:48.520 --> 05:21:57.240
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Vietnam funded their tourism, 183.43 in campaign.

asr-006350
05:21:57.240 --> 05:22:01.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Yung arrival po nila was 21.17 million.

asr-006351
05:22:02.260 --> 05:22:12.260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: And then Singapore, for $22 million, yung arrival po nila is 16.91 million people or tourists.

asr-006352
05:22:12.840 --> 05:22:13.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Indonesia, ganun din po.

asr-006353
05:22:14.340 --> 05:22:22.500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Indonesia went down actually, yung kanilang budget of 54.47,

asr-006354
05:22:22.500 --> 05:22:25.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: pero mataas pa rin po siya compared sa Philippines na,

asr-006355
05:22:25.840 --> 05:22:30.680
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: we spent last year, noong 2025, 49.72 million pesos.

asr-006356
05:22:31.120 --> 05:22:35.800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ang dumating lamang po, it was converted to about 5.87 million arrivals.

asr-006357
05:22:36.260 --> 05:22:41.220
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So medyo malaki po yung funding ng tourism promotions po natin,

asr-006358
05:22:41.620 --> 05:22:46.640
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: kung ikukumpara sa ibang bansa, hundreds of millions, tayo po ay nasa 52 million.

asr-006359
05:22:47.120 --> 05:22:50.700
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: At bumaba pa nga po noong 2025 to 49.72 million.

asr-006360
05:22:50.700 --> 05:22:55.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: And I believe these are some of the reasons, Mr. President, kung bakit.

asr-006361
05:22:55.840 --> 05:23:00.140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Mababa po yung arrivals natin because of ika nga yung campaign.

asr-006362
05:23:00.420 --> 05:23:03.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Unlike other countries na talagang sobra yung kanilang promotions.

asr-006363
05:23:04.660 --> 05:23:09.260
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes, and I think promotions, very important aspect of tourism.

asr-006364
05:23:09.940 --> 05:23:17.100
Senator Mark A. Villar: I also want to know, does the DOT conduct regular meetings with other agencies

asr-006365
05:23:17.100 --> 05:23:20.760
Senator Mark A. Villar: to discuss the concerns in our major tourist destinations?

asr-006366
05:23:20.760 --> 05:23:25.720
Senator Mark A. Villar: The reason why I'm asking is because we know that aside from the connectivity,

asr-006367
05:23:25.840 --> 05:23:31.040
Senator Mark A. Villar: yung binanggit po ni Senator Erwin, yung pagpunta sa destination,

asr-006368
05:23:31.820 --> 05:23:38.320
Senator Mark A. Villar: minsan magsustop ka pa sa Cebu bago ka makarating sa final destination mo.

asr-006369
05:23:39.000 --> 05:23:41.340
Senator Mark A. Villar: Aside from that, there are also issues with energy.

asr-006370
05:23:41.900 --> 05:23:45.980
Senator Mark A. Villar: Minsan, lalo in the islands, madalas po ang brownout.

asr-006371
05:23:45.980 --> 05:23:50.660
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, nasisira lahat ng equipments, ng mga resorts.

asr-006372
05:23:51.420 --> 05:23:54.760
Senator Mark A. Villar: We have no tax incentives similar to other countries.

asr-006373
05:23:55.160 --> 05:23:55.560
Senator Mark A. Villar: All other.

asr-006374
05:23:55.840 --> 05:23:59.860
Senator Mark A. Villar: Practically, every other country that I've been to, they offer tax rebates.

asr-006375
05:24:00.280 --> 05:24:02.860
Senator Mark A. Villar: We don't give these tax rebates.

asr-006376
05:24:03.520 --> 05:24:10.920
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, there are so many factors that combine to make our tourism less competitive.

asr-006377
05:24:10.920 --> 05:24:18.180
Senator Mark A. Villar: What I want to know is if the department is currently engaging with other departments

asr-006378
05:24:18.180 --> 05:24:21.000
Senator Mark A. Villar: such as the Department of Energy, the Department of Public Works,

asr-006379
05:24:21.100 --> 05:24:24.220
Senator Mark A. Villar: the Department of Transportation,

asr-006380
05:24:24.800 --> 05:24:25.820
Senator Mark A. Villar: in order to come up...

asr-006381
05:24:25.840 --> 05:24:27.420
Senator Mark A. Villar: In order to address these issues.

asr-006382
05:24:27.540 --> 05:24:30.680
