10:28:13.740 --> 10:28:15.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: has said that she will endeavor

asr-013120
10:28:15.360 --> 10:28:17.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: to speak to the new

asr-013121
10:28:17.400 --> 10:28:19.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: BIR commissioner about this, Mr. President.

asr-013122
10:28:19.880 --> 10:28:21.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: In many cases, the same documents

asr-013123
10:28:21.760 --> 10:28:23.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: are required and then they have to

asr-013124
10:28:23.460 --> 10:28:24.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: be delivered at the same time.

asr-013125
10:28:25.620 --> 10:28:27.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And the sellers

asr-013126
10:28:27.340 --> 10:28:29.260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: have to provide the registration

asr-013127
10:28:29.260 --> 10:28:31.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: information at great risk to themselves.

asr-013128
10:28:31.800 --> 10:28:32.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

asr-013129
10:28:32.100 --> 10:28:33.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And then

asr-013130
10:28:33.740 --> 10:28:35.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: they are

asr-013131
10:28:35.760 --> 10:28:38.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: appreciative if there would be a single

asr-013132
10:28:38.120 --> 10:28:39.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: verification link.

asr-013133
10:28:39.500 --> 10:28:42.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Paraming sana na lang at yung one exposure na

asr-013134
10:28:42.160 --> 10:28:44.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: lamang. And the question

asr-013135
10:28:44.240 --> 10:28:45.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: also arises, will the DTI

asr-013136
10:28:45.800 --> 10:28:48.320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: continue to keep the trust mark voluntary

asr-013137
10:28:48.320 --> 10:28:49.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: in light of the fact that

asr-013138
10:28:49.920 --> 10:28:50.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: BIR

asr-013139
10:28:50.640 --> 10:28:53.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: has its requirements,

asr-013140
10:28:53.460 --> 10:28:54.420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: as mandatory?

asr-013141
10:28:54.820 --> 10:28:56.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi pa pwede magkaisa na lang ang gobyerno?

asr-013142
10:28:57.120 --> 10:28:59.040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pwede ba mag-GC na lang kayo at

asr-013143
10:28:59.040 --> 10:29:00.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: minsanan matapos to?

asr-013144
10:29:01.300 --> 10:29:02.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. President, so unang-una,

asr-013145
10:29:03.020 --> 10:29:03.480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the

asr-013146
10:29:03.480 --> 10:29:07.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: trust mark will remain voluntary.

asr-013147
10:29:07.940 --> 10:29:09.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The secretary

asr-013148
10:29:09.180 --> 10:29:11.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: will endeavor to speak to the BIR

asr-013149
10:29:11.260 --> 10:29:13.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: regarding this issue. And

asr-013150
10:29:13.180 --> 10:29:15.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: they will be, excuse me,

asr-013151
10:29:15.040 --> 10:29:17.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: implementing the MSME green lanes next

asr-013152
10:29:17.240 --> 10:29:19.200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: year para itong mga requirements po

asr-013153
10:29:19.200 --> 10:29:21.140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ay mas maging madali at kaya-ayas

asr-013154
10:29:21.140 --> 10:29:22.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: para sa mga MSMEs.

asr-013155
10:29:23.460 --> 10:29:25.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi ako nakakatanggap sa mga online

asr-013156
10:29:25.700 --> 10:29:27.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: seller na sangkatutak

asr-013157
10:29:27.560 --> 10:29:30.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: na reklamo dyan. Kasi paulit-ulit.

asr-013158
10:29:30.640 --> 10:29:32.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At yung trust mark,

asr-013159
10:29:32.400 --> 10:29:34.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: sa kabila ng pagiging voluntary,

asr-013160
10:29:34.920 --> 10:29:36.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: ang concern is

asr-013161
10:29:36.800 --> 10:29:38.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: how will it protect home-based

asr-013162
10:29:38.300 --> 10:29:40.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: sellers' personal addresses?

asr-013163
10:29:40.740 --> 10:29:42.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi nandun eh, may requirement.

asr-013164
10:29:42.940 --> 10:29:44.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Eh bakit sila magpapa-expose

asr-013165
10:29:44.380 --> 10:29:46.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: ng gano'n online na nga eh?

asr-013166
10:29:46.140 --> 10:29:47.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, Mr. President,

asr-013167
10:29:47.380 --> 10:29:50.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: as the gentle lady from

asr-013168
10:29:50.160 --> 10:29:52.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ilocos Norte knows, this is always also my issue.

asr-013169
10:29:52.580 --> 10:29:53.260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yeah, tama.

asr-013170
10:29:53.260 --> 10:29:55.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Tutuwa naman nukaming nakinig yung DTI

asr-013171
10:29:55.000 --> 10:29:56.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: when we requested them to

asr-013172
10:29:56.520 --> 10:29:59.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: not be so heavy-handed with our

asr-013173
10:29:59.120 --> 10:29:59.940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: MSMEs, no?

asr-013174
10:30:00.000 --> 10:30:16.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Hindi lang po security issue, it's also a hassle and it also, my opinion, gastos but it also doesn't really assure the public that everybody with a trust mark is to be trusted.

asr-013175
10:30:16.020 --> 10:30:36.580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Correct. But in fairness, Mr. President, DTI has listened to all of us and has made it voluntary and instead of having all of these requirements, they will establish a fast track for registration and ease of doing business for our MSMEs next year, Mr. President.

asr-013176
10:30:36.580 --> 10:30:45.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's right. But the duplication with BIR, which is only temporarily suspended, remains an added onus on our business.

asr-013177
10:30:46.020 --> 10:30:48.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: For very small online sellers.

asr-013178
10:30:48.140 --> 10:30:55.040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes. Mr. President, the Secretary has committed to speak to BIR about this para nina po doble-doble yung mga requirements po.

asr-013179
10:30:55.500 --> 10:31:00.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The other question is also something that's been mysterious for many of us.

asr-013180
10:31:00.400 --> 10:31:05.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why is the trade deficit widening despite record exports?

asr-013181
10:31:06.360 --> 10:31:15.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: In September, goods exported rose by 35.6% and yet the deficit widened by 10%.

asr-013182
10:31:16.020 --> 10:31:29.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 10.3%? So it sounds like there's a loss of 45.9%? Which imports drove the wider gap? Bakit ganon? Parang baliktad, hindi namin maintindihan.

asr-013183
10:31:29.600 --> 10:31:40.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And why can't, which Philippine firms supply competitively? What are, what's missing in this configuration?

asr-013184
10:31:40.460 --> 10:31:45.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. President, so there was an increase in imports of capital goods.

asr-013185
10:31:46.020 --> 10:31:48.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Which is usually machines and equipment, as well as fuel.

asr-013186
10:31:49.140 --> 10:31:52.940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasama rin yung importation of fuel with regard to the deficit.

asr-013187
10:31:53.700 --> 10:31:56.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: With regard to the imports and export deficit.

asr-013188
10:31:56.460 --> 10:32:00.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So perhaps we could have a more complete picture if you could provide us the data.

asr-013189
10:32:01.100 --> 10:32:05.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Because what only comes out in the media is the increase by 35.6%.

asr-013190
10:32:06.060 --> 10:32:08.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It sounds good. It's good news.

asr-013191
10:32:08.500 --> 10:32:14.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pakatapos babagsakan tayo ng trade deficit of 5.15 billion US dollars.

asr-013192
10:32:14.440 --> 10:32:14.580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

asr-013193
10:32:14.580 --> 10:32:20.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Na nalilito ang taong bayan. Parang naluloko ba kayo? O talagang hindi namin maintindihan?

asr-013194
10:32:20.840 --> 10:32:23.500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. President, DTI will give your office the breakdown.

asr-013195
10:32:23.920 --> 10:32:39.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So ang sinasabi ninyo, on account of the stupendous increase in energy imports, yung exports natin na tumaas by 35.6% e nabura.

asr-013196
10:32:39.860 --> 10:32:40.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Exactly.

asr-013197
10:32:40.700 --> 10:32:41.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Parang ganon?

asr-013198
10:32:41.880 --> 10:32:42.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

asr-013199
10:32:42.300 --> 10:32:42.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

asr-013200
10:32:44.580 --> 10:32:52.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, which products and markets will DTI prioritize beyond electronics?

asr-013201
10:32:52.300 --> 10:32:55.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi parating ng electronics yung 62% na mayuwaga.

asr-013202
10:32:59.540 --> 10:33:01.680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, semiconductors.

asr-013203
10:33:01.980 --> 10:33:04.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi, I just said electronics. Pwera sa electronics.

asr-013204
10:33:05.840 --> 10:33:06.640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Minerals.

asr-013205
10:33:07.380 --> 10:33:08.660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Automotive parts.

asr-013206
10:33:09.660 --> 10:33:11.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Automotive parts, ang bigap ng tariff.

asr-013207
10:33:11.880 --> 10:33:13.360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We're non-competitive na nga.

asr-013208
10:33:13.460 --> 10:33:14.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sabi ng automotive.

asr-013209
10:33:14.580 --> 10:33:15.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Industry, eh.

asr-013210
10:33:15.980 --> 10:33:17.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: This is the report of DTI, no?

asr-013211
10:33:18.460 --> 10:33:19.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And agricultural products.

asr-013212
10:33:20.320 --> 10:33:21.940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Aling agricultural products?

asr-013213
10:33:22.260 --> 10:33:22.640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Coconut.

asr-013214
10:33:23.700 --> 10:33:27.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Coconut increased by 34% this year.

asr-013215
10:33:29.560 --> 10:33:34.320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pineapple, banana, ube, calamansi.

asr-013216
10:33:36.180 --> 10:33:38.980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And they will be pushing bamboo as well, Mr. President.

asr-013217
10:33:38.980 --> 10:33:39.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

asr-013218
10:33:39.500 --> 10:33:41.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Palibasa nga, nabanggit yung coconut.

asr-013219
10:33:41.440 --> 10:33:43.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sana tulungan na ng CF.

asr-013220
10:33:44.580 --> 10:33:48.680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: FIDP yung funding ng CDA sa mga coconut farmer co-ops.

asr-013221
10:33:48.800 --> 10:33:51.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Matagal na nag-iintay yung mga sa Mindanao, eh.

asr-013222
10:33:53.100 --> 10:33:57.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, we would appreciate also the breakdown there

asr-013223
10:33:57.100 --> 10:34:03.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: because I think the public would appreciate full understanding of this phenomenon

asr-013224
10:34:03.120 --> 10:34:06.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: that the trade deficit keeps widening and we keep exporting.

asr-013225
10:34:06.800 --> 10:34:08.200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: They will submit, Mr. President.

asr-013226
10:34:08.220 --> 10:34:09.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Parang nga, they don't put the two things together.

asr-013227
10:34:10.140 --> 10:34:14.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Isa pa, what is the plan for the BPO workers whose jobs are affected by AIDA?

asr-013228
10:34:14.460 --> 10:34:19.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Alam naman natin, ang sabi nila, maraming untrainable na.

asr-013229
10:34:19.980 --> 10:34:22.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kailangan naman yung iba, upskilling.

asr-013230
10:34:23.060 --> 10:34:26.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung iba talaga, wala na talagang trabaho dahil sa AI.

asr-013231
10:34:27.360 --> 10:34:33.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, what roles will be the most exposed?

asr-013232
10:34:34.040 --> 10:34:35.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Which are the most vulnerable?

asr-013233
10:34:35.440 --> 10:34:36.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Para alam natin.

asr-013234
10:34:36.580 --> 10:34:41.980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. President, so I had a hearing about this, Mr. President, recently or a few months ago.

asr-013235
10:34:41.980 --> 10:34:44.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: At alam mo natin na,

asr-013236
10:34:44.460 --> 10:34:46.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: BPO industry natin is really at risk, no?

asr-013237
10:34:47.320 --> 10:34:53.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The first jobs that will be lost are the voice and the lower skilled, no?

asr-013238
10:34:53.960 --> 10:34:58.760
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Compared to the more complex type of BPO industry work.

asr-013239
10:34:58.780 --> 10:35:01.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Eh, isang katutak ang ating call center.

asr-013240
10:35:01.500 --> 10:35:01.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Exactly.

asr-013241
10:35:02.440 --> 10:35:09.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The industry itself, Mr. President, nagbanggit na year on year, tumataas pa naman tayo by 5% this year.

asr-013242
10:35:09.440 --> 10:35:14.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But what I had raised as an issue to them is that if you break down the subsector,

asr-013243
10:35:14.460 --> 10:35:19.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: of the BPO industry, makikita na malaki yung pagbagsak sa ibang mga subsector.

asr-013244
10:35:19.960 --> 10:35:25.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And that even though we are increasing as a whole, yung mga nawala ng trabaho in a particular subsector,

asr-013245
10:35:26.000 --> 10:35:31.960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: kunyari voice, hindi naman yun yung mga trabahong bago na dadagdag.

asr-013246
10:35:32.120 --> 10:35:34.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, even that subsector needs our support, no?

asr-013247
10:35:34.960 --> 10:35:38.820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, napag-usapan po doon yung mga social safety net programs.

asr-013248
10:35:39.440 --> 10:35:41.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But apart from that, is the…

asr-013249
10:35:41.120 --> 10:35:42.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, but Ayuda only goes so far.

asr-013250
10:35:42.980 --> 10:35:43.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Exactly.

asr-013251
10:35:43.240 --> 10:35:44.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ayuda is not a new job.

asr-013252
10:35:44.400 --> 10:35:57.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Apart from that, Mr. President, TESDA and DICT, so this is not with DTI, but TESDA and DICT currently have funding for their upskilling programs na matagal na rin ho namin kinukulit na kailangan na nilang gawin.

asr-013253
10:35:58.280 --> 10:36:10.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There is a promotion of high-value IT services, and again, this is to really quote-unquote upskill our workers in animation, game development, healthcare information management, and so on and so forth.

asr-013254
10:36:10.740 --> 10:36:13.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But I joined the…

asr-013255
10:36:14.400 --> 10:36:26.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Gentlelady from Ilocos Norte in raising a concern that much like the development of AI in the world, potentially po, baka mabilis rin po yung detriment nito sa ating bansa.

asr-013256
10:36:26.440 --> 10:36:35.200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, I'm sure the Secretary and the other Secretaries are talking about this, but we need to prepare better for this eventuality, Mr. President.

asr-013257
10:36:35.200 --> 10:36:42.680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The reason I ask is I haven't seen in either TESDA or DICT's budgets anything to do with upskilling specifically.

asr-013258
10:36:43.280 --> 10:36:44.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It's still the same.

asr-013259
10:36:44.400 --> 10:36:48.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: DPO, animation, etc. Wala namang bago yata tungkol sa AI.

asr-013260
10:36:49.260 --> 10:36:56.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It was in last year's budget, Mr. President. I'm not handling those agencies, but we will check if it's there.

asr-013261
10:36:56.900 --> 10:37:00.660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But meron pong specific line items yan in the 2026 budget.

asr-013262
10:37:01.640 --> 10:37:04.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 2026? Pero 2027 andong pa rin?

asr-013263
10:37:04.380 --> 10:37:07.960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We will check, Mr. President. But again, I'm not handling those agencies, but we will check.

asr-013264
10:37:07.960 --> 10:37:11.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero wala sa DTI, kaya siguro wala akong nakikita.

asr-013265
10:37:12.520 --> 10:37:13.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Which are the most…

asr-013266
10:37:14.400 --> 10:37:16.360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The most vulnerable, yung pinaka-low-end.

asr-013267
10:37:16.940 --> 10:37:20.100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Well, I don't want to call them low-end, but the majority are voice.

asr-013268
10:37:20.380 --> 10:37:22.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Well, lowest paid, I mean, obviously.

asr-013269
10:37:23.480 --> 10:37:25.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's the most vulnerable, Mr. President.

asr-013270
10:37:26.060 --> 10:37:32.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Are there already employers committed to hiring graduates of these upskilling programs?

asr-013271
10:37:33.340 --> 10:37:36.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi syempre, pag nag-upskill yan, dapat may sasalo, no?

asr-013272
10:37:37.180 --> 10:37:40.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Right now, Mr. President, meron namang spasyo. And again, this is from my hearing.

asr-013273
10:37:40.780 --> 10:37:42.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I don't think DTI is really…

asr-013274
10:37:43.280 --> 10:37:43.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sure.

asr-013275
10:37:43.460 --> 10:37:46.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I don't think they're really on top of this. It's really DICT and TESTA.

asr-013276
10:37:46.360 --> 10:37:49.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The BPO hires so many of our labor force.

asr-013277
10:37:49.740 --> 10:37:51.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: As an industry, as an industry…

asr-013278
10:37:52.160 --> 10:37:53.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: They're still regulated by them.

asr-013279
10:37:55.020 --> 10:38:01.220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: They take care of the industry, but in terms of the upskilling, the funding is with DICT and TESTA.

asr-013280
10:38:01.220 --> 10:38:09.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, you said that. So what options are available? Failing upskilling, kasi yung iba hindi naman pwede mag-upskill, at saka ilan lang yung programa.

asr-013281
10:38:09.460 --> 10:38:13.440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What options are available for workers who need to move outside BPO?

asr-013282
10:38:13.460 --> 10:38:22.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. President, let me share, in that hearing that we had, meron kaming nakausap na may-ari ng isang maliit na call center sa Cebu.

asr-013283
10:38:23.460 --> 10:38:33.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Only 150 seats, 200 seats. And when I visited her, their call center agents were training the AI that will eventually replace them.

asr-013284
10:38:33.920 --> 10:38:34.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Oh, okay.

asr-013285
10:38:34.300 --> 10:38:36.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Can you imagine that? Yung trabaho po nila…

asr-013286
10:38:36.900 --> 10:38:38.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: No, but somebody needs to do it.

asr-013287
10:38:38.620 --> 10:38:39.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: No, exactly.

asr-013288
10:38:39.420 --> 10:38:42.360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Because naghahalusinate nga yung AI hanggang ngayon.

asr-013289
10:38:42.360 --> 10:38:43.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, but…

asr-013290
10:38:43.460 --> 10:38:46.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: They're basically working on their obsolescence, no? Yung call center na ito.

asr-013291
10:38:46.340 --> 10:38:51.980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: When I asked her, ano yung plano niya, ang sagot niya sa akin, catering. Like, mag-iiba talaga siya ng industriya.

asr-013292
10:38:52.120 --> 10:38:52.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Totally.

asr-013293
10:38:52.800 --> 10:38:55.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And when I saw her again a few months later, caterer na siya.

asr-013294
10:38:55.620 --> 10:38:55.940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay.

asr-013295
10:38:55.940 --> 10:39:00.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, there's really a lot of risk here, Mr. President.

asr-013296
10:39:01.120 --> 10:39:07.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And alongside yourself, I've been trying to really…

asr-013297
10:39:07.400 --> 10:39:13.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kung bagay yung sa Tagalog, kinakalampag ho natin na we need to be able to really do more in terms of those who…

asr-013298
10:39:13.460 --> 10:39:16.480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: who might lose their jobs. Ang takot ko po dito…

asr-013299
10:39:16.480 --> 10:39:17.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Because it's a huge number.

asr-013300
10:39:18.060 --> 10:39:19.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It's a huge number, Mr. President.

asr-013301
10:39:19.240 --> 10:39:20.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We're talking of upwards of a million.

asr-013302
10:39:20.340 --> 10:39:21.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And if I may add…

asr-013303
10:39:21.120 --> 10:39:24.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Na ma-dislocate. Napakarami niyan. Hindi naman pwede mag-cater.

asr-013304
10:39:25.080 --> 10:39:29.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Napakarami as a whole. But if you look at it, Mr. President, per city.

asr-013305
10:39:29.620 --> 10:39:32.040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi nagkaroon tayo ng next wave cities implementation.

asr-013306
10:39:32.040 --> 10:39:32.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kaya nga, yung breakdown per city.

asr-013307
10:39:33.080 --> 10:39:36.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pag bin-breakdown niyo po yun per city, kahit isang call center sa isang syudad magsara,

asr-013308
10:39:37.060 --> 10:39:39.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 1,000 ka agad yan na mawawala ng trabaho.

asr-013309
10:39:39.540 --> 10:39:41.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tapos times five. Kasi yung kada pamilya.

asr-013310
10:39:41.580 --> 10:39:43.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, may pamilya.

asr-013311
10:39:43.460 --> 10:39:45.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Plus yung related industries.

asr-013312
10:39:45.640 --> 10:39:49.680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung mga kumikita dyan because of the eateries, because of transportation.

asr-013313
10:39:50.600 --> 10:39:53.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, this is something we really have to look at, Mr. President.

asr-013314
10:39:53.480 --> 10:39:54.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mahalaga talaga ito.

asr-013315
10:39:54.560 --> 10:40:00.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And honestly, maganda pong na-bring up niyo ito because I honestly feel that

asr-013316
10:40:00.240 --> 10:40:02.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the executive really needs to focus on this a little bit more.

asr-013317
10:40:03.700 --> 10:40:09.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It's not really with DTI per se, but definitely, kung meron pong industriya na magkakaproblema,

asr-013318
10:40:09.360 --> 10:40:10.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: it will be DTI's concern.

asr-013319
10:40:10.620 --> 10:40:12.700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, right now, DTI…

asr-013320
10:40:12.700 --> 10:40:22.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: From the Secretary, provides market access for MSMEs, supply exporters, but in terms of this…

asr-013321
10:40:22.880 --> 10:40:24.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I think we have to provide a little more than market access.

asr-013322
10:40:25.080 --> 10:40:28.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Surely, there should be an industry roadmap for BPO.

asr-013323
10:40:29.200 --> 10:40:31.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: A little more than market access is required.

asr-013324
10:40:31.640 --> 10:40:31.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. President, you know…

asr-013325
10:40:31.880 --> 10:40:34.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And I think that's within DTI's mandate.

asr-013326
10:40:34.400 --> 10:40:38.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, and let me add, during the time that roadmap was being made,

asr-013327
10:40:38.260 --> 10:40:42.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I don't think the level of advancement of AI was considered…

asr-013328
10:40:42.520 --> 10:40:44.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: By roadmap, I mean a new one.

asr-013329
10:40:44.360 --> 10:40:45.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi na pwede talaga yun dati.

asr-013330
10:40:45.900 --> 10:40:47.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, I get that, Mr. President.

asr-013331
10:40:47.900 --> 10:40:48.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Who's in charge of that?

asr-013332
10:40:48.660 --> 10:40:49.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The BOI, ba, is in charge of that?

asr-013333
10:40:50.160 --> 10:40:54.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, Yusek Perio is a regular guest here already in the Senate.

asr-013334
10:40:55.060 --> 10:40:58.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: He's nodding his head that they will take a look at that.

asr-013335
10:40:58.120 --> 10:41:01.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Parang wala pa tayong nakikita ng AI roadmap.

asr-013336
10:41:01.260 --> 10:41:02.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nakaka-nervous eh.

asr-013337
10:41:02.220 --> 10:41:02.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang daming BPO.

asr-013338
10:41:03.020 --> 10:41:03.420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Meron.

asr-013339
10:41:03.980 --> 10:41:04.980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Merong AI roadmap.

asr-013340
10:41:06.360 --> 10:41:06.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pero…

asr-013341
10:41:06.920 --> 10:41:10.040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But I'm afraid that it might not be up to par with the advancements.

asr-013342
10:41:10.220 --> 10:41:10.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's my concern.

asr-013343
10:41:11.060 --> 10:41:11.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At saka hindi siya…

asr-013344
10:41:12.520 --> 10:41:14.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Masinop tungkol sa employment.

asr-013345
10:41:14.880 --> 10:41:15.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Eh, yun ang mahalaga.

asr-013346
10:41:16.080 --> 10:41:16.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, Mr. President.

asr-013347
10:41:17.020 --> 10:41:19.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Last year, hawak ko yung budget ng DTI.

asr-013348
10:41:19.680 --> 10:41:21.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And laging pinagtatanungan.

asr-013349
10:41:22.320 --> 10:41:25.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Eh, yun tungkol sa CIAP.

asr-013350
10:41:26.320 --> 10:41:29.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ito yung Contractors Association.

asr-013351
10:41:30.340 --> 10:41:32.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At pakatapos ng flood control,

asr-013352
10:41:32.880 --> 10:41:36.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: lahat nagulat na yung DTI pala ang regulatory agency

asr-013353
10:41:37.340 --> 10:41:39.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: para sa lahat ng kontratista ng Pilipinas.

asr-013354
10:41:40.060 --> 10:41:41.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At that point in time,

asr-013355
10:41:41.440 --> 10:41:41.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: iisa lang yung…

asr-013356
10:41:42.520 --> 10:41:46.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ito yung number nung contracting industry.

asr-013357
10:41:48.520 --> 10:41:49.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dumami na ba yung member?

asr-013358
10:41:49.960 --> 10:41:50.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nakompleto na ba?

asr-013359
10:41:50.900 --> 10:41:51.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: May quorum na ba?

asr-013360
10:41:51.880 --> 10:41:52.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Is it functional?

asr-013361
10:41:53.760 --> 10:41:55.420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: This is the PCAB, Mr. President.

asr-013362
10:41:55.500 --> 10:41:56.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's right.

asr-013363
10:41:56.160 --> 10:41:56.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The PCAB.

asr-013364
10:41:57.540 --> 10:42:00.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The PCAB has a CIAP on top of it,

asr-013365
10:42:00.540 --> 10:42:02.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: which is a regulatory including DTI.

asr-013366
10:42:03.540 --> 10:42:05.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The PCAB is now complete, Mr. President.

asr-013367
10:42:05.700 --> 10:42:06.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kompleto na siya.

asr-013368
10:42:06.580 --> 10:42:08.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And yung CIAP, kompleto na rin.

asr-013369
10:42:09.220 --> 10:42:10.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Also complete, Mr. President.

asr-013370
10:42:10.440 --> 10:42:12.440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Also, meron na ba tayong…

asr-013371
10:42:12.520 --> 10:42:16.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Meron na ba tayong rules to verify that the contractor has enough working capital,

asr-013372
10:42:17.020 --> 10:42:19.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: has no backlog, has no…

asr-013373
10:42:19.560 --> 10:42:20.600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Stricter implementation.

asr-013374
10:42:21.380 --> 10:42:23.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There is stricter implementation now, Mr. President.

asr-013375
10:42:24.120 --> 10:42:25.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: This is coming from the Secretary.

asr-013376
10:42:26.040 --> 10:42:30.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Under implementation, paano mag-iimplement nung nakaraan taon,

asr-013377
10:42:30.420 --> 10:42:32.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: wala pa ngang IRR na bago.

asr-013378
10:42:32.740 --> 10:42:33.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Walang revised.

asr-013379
10:42:33.760 --> 10:42:35.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: They were required to revise,

asr-013380
10:42:36.020 --> 10:42:41.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: but as many times as we requested them to submit the revised rules,

asr-013381
10:42:41.480 --> 10:42:42.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: wala naman na.

asr-013382
10:42:42.520 --> 10:42:47.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, I don't know what they're implementing kasi hindi pwede yung lumang rules.

asr-013383
10:42:47.380 --> 10:42:48.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Talagang hindi po pwede yun.

asr-013384
10:42:48.920 --> 10:42:52.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. President, may clarify, wala hong nabigay ang CIAP o walang nabigay ang DTI?

asr-013385
10:42:53.220 --> 10:42:54.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung PCAB.

asr-013386
10:42:54.560 --> 10:42:55.220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung DTI.

asr-013387
10:42:55.360 --> 10:43:02.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: DTI in general was supposed to give that kasi nga it became very, very controversial

asr-013388
10:43:02.700 --> 10:43:07.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: na yung mga blacklisted, pinapayagan pa rin.

asr-013389
10:43:07.780 --> 10:43:11.680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung mga walang puhunan, walang equipment, andun pa rin.

asr-013390
10:43:11.680 --> 10:43:12.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung qualified pa rin.

asr-013391
10:43:13.160 --> 10:43:17.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tapos, yung mga contractors dealing with so many public works contracts,

asr-013392
10:43:17.900 --> 10:43:18.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: andun pa rin.

asr-013393
10:43:19.060 --> 10:43:22.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Who checks the equipment, the plant, and the personnel?

asr-013394
10:43:23.020 --> 10:43:24.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, according to the Secretary, Mr. President,

asr-013395
10:43:24.940 --> 10:43:26.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: they're doing stricter implementation.

asr-013396
10:43:26.580 --> 10:43:29.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: They'll submit the rules, but right now,

asr-013397
10:43:29.240 --> 10:43:32.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The rules are still the same or they've been revised finally?

asr-013398
10:43:33.060 --> 10:43:37.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: They're revised, and right now, nagtanggal na sila ng conflict of interest.

asr-013399
10:43:37.920 --> 10:43:39.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang daming conflict of interest.

asr-013400
10:43:39.280 --> 10:43:41.040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung nakaupo, puro kontratista.

asr-013401
10:43:41.680 --> 10:43:46.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, right now, contractors are no longer allowed to sit in the PCAB.

asr-013402
10:43:46.760 --> 10:43:47.420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Oh, that's good.

asr-013403
10:43:47.800 --> 10:43:52.680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And what action does the PCAB take if a contractor misrepresents its resources

asr-013404
10:43:52.680 --> 10:43:56.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: or no longer meets its license requirements?

asr-013405
10:43:59.640 --> 10:44:03.660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, they're not given the license if they don't meet the requirements, Mr. President?

asr-013406
10:44:03.660 --> 10:44:04.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yun nga, but somewhere along the line.

asr-013407
10:44:04.900 --> 10:44:06.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yun pala, naghiraman.

asr-013408
10:44:06.540 --> 10:44:09.360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Diba, uso yan yung naghihiraman ng lisensya.

asr-013409
10:44:09.580 --> 10:44:11.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Usong-uso yan sa flood control, diba?

asr-013410
10:44:11.680 --> 10:44:19.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: From the time that the PCAB was put under the office of the Secretary,

asr-013411
10:44:19.600 --> 10:44:20.980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the Secretary's been very...

asr-013412
10:44:20.980 --> 10:44:22.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: No, it's always been under DTI.

asr-013413
10:44:23.200 --> 10:44:26.660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Siguro, to put it in other words, when the scandal broke out,

asr-013414
10:44:26.720 --> 10:44:28.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: and now that the Secretary's really on top of it,

asr-013415
10:44:28.780 --> 10:44:32.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: she's been very focused on the implementation of these new rules, Mr. President.

asr-013416
10:44:33.440 --> 10:44:33.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

asr-013417
10:44:34.780 --> 10:44:39.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I'm a little perplexed that the implementation came ahead of the revision of the rules,

asr-013418
10:44:39.120 --> 10:44:40.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: but okay.

asr-013419
10:44:41.680 --> 10:44:46.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: If we could see the new rules, because the previous ones were clearly inadequate

asr-013420
10:44:46.020 --> 10:44:47.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: because they got away with murder.

asr-013421
10:44:49.000 --> 10:44:53.940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There are rules that were agreed on, and they will submit to your office, Mr. President.

asr-013422
10:44:54.320 --> 10:44:54.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yeah.

asr-013423
10:44:54.600 --> 10:44:58.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I think they should submit to the body because we are supposed to undertake investigations

asr-013424
10:44:58.820 --> 10:45:03.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and we're incapable of doing so until we know what rules are being violated.

asr-013425
10:45:03.300 --> 10:45:03.960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, Mr. President.

asr-013425-insert-1
10:45:04.160 --> 10:45:29.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay, so we were all agitated by the 100% import declared by President Donald Trump in the White House Conference following his visit to ASEAN and APEC. 100% of the Philippines' energy and agricultural imports were derived from the United States. The DFA said that it has since been assigned to the DTI.

asr-013426
10:45:30.000 --> 10:45:36.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, Secretary Roque, what is this deal that has been concluded?

asr-013427
10:45:37.280 --> 10:45:41.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What commitments, if any, has Manila made on purchase volumes,

asr-013428
10:45:41.960 --> 10:45:47.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: the exclusive sourcing that was declared, and what is the impact on the tariff?

asr-013429
10:45:47.260 --> 10:45:51.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, Mr. President, the Secretary has informed me that negotiations are ongoing.

asr-013430
10:45:51.600 --> 10:45:52.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Nothing's been agreed.

asr-013431
10:45:53.240 --> 10:45:57.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And they don't want to divulge the ongoing negotiations.

asr-013432
10:45:57.160 --> 10:45:59.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Well, President Trump has already divulged.

asr-013433
10:45:59.520 --> 10:46:05.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But I myself will say, Mr. President, maybe the Secretary is undergoing negotiations.

asr-013434
10:46:05.260 --> 10:46:06.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I don't think that's even feasible.

asr-013435
10:46:07.060 --> 10:46:08.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I don't think that's even feasible.

asr-013436
10:46:09.580 --> 10:46:12.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But right now, the Secretary is saying negotiations are ongoing.

asr-013437
10:46:12.740 --> 10:46:15.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Nothing's been agreed.

asr-013438
10:46:15.760 --> 10:46:20.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But, Mr. President, it is the role of the Senate to also find out what this is.

asr-013439
10:46:21.460 --> 10:46:26.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's why I've actually filed a resolution, which is why I'm taking the opportunity to ask.

asr-013440
10:46:26.460 --> 10:46:29.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: If it gets sent to my committee,

asr-013441
10:46:29.280 --> 10:46:31.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: we can take a look at that, Mr. President.

asr-013442
10:46:31.840 --> 10:46:38.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kung sa trade siya pupunta, we can have a hearing about that para we can ask the Secretary and the other agencies

asr-013443
10:46:38.160 --> 10:46:41.080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: to share with us where they are in terms of negotiations.

asr-013444
10:46:41.560 --> 10:46:46.100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Because in the end, all of these negotiations will be a treaty, and we will also have to sign off on it anyway.

asr-013445
10:46:46.400 --> 10:46:48.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, we might as well find out from now.

asr-013446
10:46:48.340 --> 10:46:50.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But, honestly, Mr. President, nung nalaman ko yan,

asr-013447
10:46:50.360 --> 10:46:54.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: pero nung nalaman ko yan, Mr. President, ang una kong tanong,

asr-013448
10:46:54.000 --> 10:46:55.140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: is that even possible?

asr-013449
10:46:55.320 --> 10:46:59.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I don't think it's even really possible to have all of your employees,

asr-013450
10:46:59.280 --> 10:47:00.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: reports coming from one country.

asr-013451
10:47:01.680 --> 10:47:06.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pero tama ka, Mr. President, maganda nga na malaman na rin ng Senado ano ba yung parameters nito.

asr-013452
10:47:07.180 --> 10:47:07.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sige.

asr-013453
10:47:07.480 --> 10:47:15.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: In the realm of the possible, there was a proposed reduction of the 12.5 tariffs to 10%.

asr-013454
10:47:15.460 --> 10:47:16.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: May nangyari ba doon?

asr-013455
10:47:18.140 --> 10:47:20.100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Also part of the negotiations, Mr. President.

asr-013456
10:47:21.180 --> 10:47:22.200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, wala rin?

asr-013457
10:47:22.300 --> 10:47:22.420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Wala.

asr-013458
10:47:22.920 --> 10:47:26.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Naku, sa ginastos natin na bilyon-bilyon, walang sigurado?

asr-013459
10:47:27.820 --> 10:47:29.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ongoing negotiations, Mr. President.

asr-013460
10:47:29.280 --> 10:47:30.480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Coming from the Secretary.

asr-013461
10:47:30.980 --> 10:47:33.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi pala sulit yung ating gastos, pambira.

asr-013462
10:47:34.480 --> 10:47:35.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: O, sige, last question na lang.

asr-013463
10:47:35.960 --> 10:47:38.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Magkano ang noche buena sa taong ito?

asr-013464
10:47:44.640 --> 10:47:49.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. President, wala pa silang number kasi kausap pa lang nila yung mga manufacturers,

asr-013465
10:47:49.380 --> 10:47:50.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: but they commit to send to you.

asr-013466
10:47:50.840 --> 10:47:54.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I'm also interested to find out magkano ba yung bilang na yun.

asr-013467
10:47:55.800 --> 10:47:59.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi katakot-takot na mura upa ka.

asr-013468
10:47:59.280 --> 10:48:00.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, they will...

asr-013469
10:48:00.280 --> 10:48:08.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Bashing ang inabutan ko at ako'y nagtanggol ng DTI, tapos inupak-upakan kami doon sa 500 pesos.

asr-013470
10:48:08.460 --> 10:48:09.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yun lang, gusto kong malaman.

asr-013471
10:48:10.180 --> 10:48:12.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Wala pa pong number, Mr. President, but they will come up with a number.

asr-013472
10:48:12.380 --> 10:48:13.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Para ikaw naman ang maupakan.

asr-013473
10:48:14.640 --> 10:48:17.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Then, Mr. President, we will look at the list.

asr-013474
10:48:17.840 --> 10:48:18.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I also don't know...

asr-013475
10:48:18.740 --> 10:48:21.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: They will come out with the list of noche buena prices.

asr-013476
10:48:21.520 --> 10:48:26.200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: They will come out with the noche buena list by first week of December?

asr-013477
10:48:27.160 --> 10:48:28.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: By the end of the month.

asr-013480
10:48:28.480 --> 10:48:30.980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And then we can all look at it together, Mr. President.

asr-013481
10:48:31.500 --> 10:48:33.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Maraming salamat. Yun lang po.

asr-013482
10:48:33.260 --> 10:48:34.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you. Thank you, Senator Marcos.

asr-013483
10:48:35.120 --> 10:48:37.540
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Senator Aimee Marcos.

asr-013484
10:48:37.640 --> 10:48:39.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Next will be Senator Robin Padilla.

asr-013485
10:48:42.400 --> 10:48:44.360
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Maraming salamat po, Ginong Pangulo.

asr-013486
10:48:46.480 --> 10:48:47.360
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Ginong sponsor.

asr-013487
10:48:48.160 --> 10:48:50.680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Magandang gabi. Malapit ng magandang umaga, Senator.

asr-013488
10:48:50.940 --> 10:48:51.740
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Opo. Opo.

asr-013489
10:48:52.440 --> 10:48:55.700
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Yung atin pong mga bisita ay inaantok na rin.

asr-013490
10:48:55.780 --> 10:48:56.740
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Pasensya na po kayo.

asr-013491
10:48:57.360 --> 10:48:58.960
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Kailangan po namin gawin yung aming trabaho.

asr-013492
10:48:58.960 --> 10:49:04.100
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: At kami naman po'y matagal ng partner ng DTI.

asr-013493
10:49:05.120 --> 10:49:09.760
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Ako po ay kasama sa naupakan dyan sa noche buena na yan.

asr-013494
10:49:11.380 --> 10:49:13.460
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Pinirito rin po kami dyan ng asawa ko.

asr-013495
10:49:14.900 --> 10:49:19.620
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Pero ito pong mga katanungan ko ay sasummarize ko na lang po.

asr-013496
10:49:19.720 --> 10:49:20.720
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Dahil makapal-kapal to.

asr-013497
10:49:20.860 --> 10:49:24.680
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Dahil ayoko naman pong kunin yung inyong masyadong oras.

asr-013498
10:49:24.820 --> 10:49:26.600
Senator Robinhood C. Padilla: Mga tanong na lang po tungkol sa budget.

asr-013499
10:49:27.260 --> 10:49:27.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

asr-013500
